oves-required-checks message; if ACK_RESTORE_REPLACES_REQUIRED_CHECK_CONTEXT emit the replaces-context message.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-MAJ-004\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Workflow guard test harness (run_workflow_guard_case inline script, line ~206) is missing 024B-extras-2 from the tooling-slice case list; production workflow is correct but no test verifies 024B-extras-2 short-circuit path.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"test file line ~206: case $slice_id in 024A|024B-core|024B-extras|024G) — 024B-extras-2 absent. Production .github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml lines 67-76: 024A|024B-core|024B-extras|024B-extras-2|024G correctly present. No run_workflow_guard_case test exercises a 024B-extras-2 DISPATCH-NOTE path. TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-WORKFLOW-PIN-BASE-BRANCH-001.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"A PR touching docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/DISPATCH-NOTE.md would be incorrectly treated as cohort by the test harness, masking any regression where production workflow short-circuit fails. TF not addressed.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add 024B-extras-2 to the inline script's case list and add a run_workflow_guard_case test that sends a 024B-extras-2 DISPATCH-NOTE path and asserts enforce=false + Tooling slice message.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-MAJ-005\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"No context-order-shuffled test for set-equality verify phase; TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ-001 explicitly requires this test case and DISPATCH-NOTE lists restore-set-equality(context-order-shuffled) as covered.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Searched test file for shuffled/set-equality/context-order test: not found. Existing tests (restore-checks-canonical-plus-extra, restore-checks-canonical) have AFTER contexts in identical order to pre-state. The jq sort==sort at script line 1094-1099 is logically correct but the shuffled-order path is untested. DISPATCH-NOTE scope claims this test exists.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Contract between DISPATCH-NOTE claimed coverage and actual test coverage is broken. If a regression introduced order-sensitive comparison, the shuffle case would silently fail in production.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a restore test case where pre-state contexts are [context-a, context-b] and after.json returns [context-b, context-a]; assert verification passes.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-MAJ-006\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification is silently accepted as a no-op when no prior restore evidence is present; D-048 states the bypass is only allowed when prior_restore_evidence_present returns true, and DISPATCH-NOTE claims a no-prior-evidence test exists.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh check_forward_mode_safety(): ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION is checked only inside the if prior_restore_evidence_present block (lines 707-721). Without prior evidence, the flag produces no CAUTION, no sleep, no error. No test in test file exercises this path. D-048: 'bypass is only allowed when prior_restore_evidence_present returns true'. DISPATCH-NOTE: 'enable-no-gate-2-verification (mutex, no-prior-evidence)'.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"A cold-start operator who mistakenly passes --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification receives no feedback that the flag is inappropriate; declarative D-048 constraint is unenforceable. Missing test per DISPATCH-NOTE scope.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add an explicit rejection (exit 2) when ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION=1 but prior_restore_evidence_present returns false, and add a test asserting this exit 2.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-MIN-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-STAGED-RESTORE-TEST-001 not addressed: no explicit test for staged (git-added but uncommitted) prior-restore evidence detection.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Test enable-working-tree-prior-restore (line 4310) modifies the log file in the working tree without git-add; no test stages with git add before running. prior_restore_evidence_present() uses git diff HEAD which covers staged changes, but this behavior is untested.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Low risk — git diff HEAD semantically covers staged changes — but the TF contract is not satisfied. A future refactor that switches to git diff (unstaged only) would silently miss staged evidence.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a test that does git add on the modified log before invoking enable-required-check.sh without --expected-wrapper-sha, asserting exit 2 with prior --restore evidence detected.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-MIN-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-PUT-BODY-SHAPE-ASSERTIONS-001 not addressed: PUT body jq assertions present only in force-pushes, deletions, and null-status-checks tests; canonical-context, wrong-context-ack, and log-sanitization tests do not assert PUT body contents.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Tests restore-checks-canonical (line 3015), restore-log-sanitization (line 2458), restore-checks-embedded-comma (line 2917) check exit code and stdout but do not assert put-body.json contents. TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-PUT-BODY-SHAPE-ASSERTIONS-001 explicitly tracks this gap.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"A transform regression that corrupts the PUT body shape would not be caught by the context-guard tests, which only verify CAUTION emission and exit codes.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add jq assertions on $fake_gh_dir/put-body.json in restore-checks-canonical, restore-checks-wrong-context-ack, and restore-checks-embedded-comma tests to assert the full required_status_checks shape.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-MIN-003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-POLICY-CHECK-TARGET-FILTER-TESTS-001 not addressed: workflow path filter (docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[C-Z]*/**) behavior untested for boundary slice IDs.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"check-invocation-log-entry.yml paths trigger on 024[C-Z]*/** but workflow guard tests only test 024B-extras and 024C. Slices like 024G (tooling) and edge cases for pattern matching are not covered. No test verifies that a 024B-extras-2 path triggers the workflow at all.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Workflow path filter correctness for 024G and any future alphabetically-later tooling slice is unverified.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add run_workflow_guard_case test for 024G DISPATCH-NOTE path to verify tooling short-circuit and for 024D/024E/024F to verify cohort enforcement path.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-nit-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Forward-mode log block emits two blank lines when both GATE2_CAUTION_LINE and WRAPPER_INACCESSIBLE_CAUTION_LINE are empty, between - **Plan-only:** no and - **PUT payload applied:**.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh lines 1210-1211: ${GATE2_CAUTION_LINE} and ${WRAPPER_INACCESSIBLE_CAUTION_LINE} on separate lines in the heredoc; when both are empty strings, two empty lines appear in the markdown log block output.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Cosmetic: emitted log block has inconsistent blank-line count depending on flag usage, which may confuse operators comparing log entries.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Guard each line: only emit when non-empty, e.g. [ -n \\\\\\\"$GATE2_CAUTION_LINE\\\\\\\" ] && printf '%s\\\\\\\\n' \\\\\\\"$GATE2_CAUTION_LINE\\\\\\\".\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-nit-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Annotated-tag dereference only handles one level of indirection; a tag object pointing to another tag object (doubly-annotated) will not resolve to the commit SHA.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh lines 638-644: gh api git/tags/<sha> --jq .object.sha returns the sha the tag points to. For a doubly-annotated tag, .object.sha is the inner tag sha, not the commit. The comparison if [ \\\\\\\"$annotated_commit_sha\\\\\\\" = \\\\\\\"$expected_sha\\\\\\\" ] then fails. SCP release tags are unlikely to be doubly-annotated but the limitation is undocumented.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"If SCP ever uses doubly-annotated tags for releases, --expected-wrapper-sha would fail to validate them even when the SHA is a valid release.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Document the single-level dereference limitation in the function header comment, or add a recursive follow for obj_type == 'tag'.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"carry_forward_tf_status\\\": {\\n    \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ-001\\\": \\\"OPEN — set-equality jq logic is correct but context-order-shuffled test missing (CORR-MAJ-005)\\\",\\n    \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-PATH-CONTAINMENT-001\\\": \\\"OPEN — no path containment guard on RESTORE_PRE_STATE (CORR-MAJ-002)\\\",\\n    \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-COHORT-REGEX-MULTICHAR-001\\\": \\\"CLOSED — workflow grep regex 024[A-Za-z][^/]* correctly matches 024B-extras-2; --tooling-slice-id enum includes 024B-extras-2\\\",\\n    \\\"TF-024B-STEP7-FIXTURE-SEQ-001\\\": \\\"OUT-OF-SCOPE for this slice (tooling only, no step-7 demo in 024B-extras-2)\\\",\\n    \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-STAGED-RESTORE-TEST-001\\\": \\\"OPEN — no staged-evidence test (CORR-MIN-001)\\\",\\n    \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-FILE-TOCTOU-001\\\": \\\"OPEN — RESTORE_PRE_STATE opened twice without hardening; low exploitability given bootstrap-only context; not flagged as MAJ\\\",\\n    \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-WORKFLOW-PIN-BASE-BRANCH-001\\\": \\\"OPEN — test harness inline script missing 024B-extras-2 (CORR-MAJ-004)\\\",\\n    \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-POLICY-CHECK-TARGET-FILTER-TESTS-001\\\": \\\"OPEN — boundary path filter tests missing (CORR-MIN-003)\\\",\\n    \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-PUT-BODY-SHAPE-ASSERTIONS-001\\\": \\\"OPEN — PUT body assertions absent in most restore tests (CORR-MIN-002)\\\",\\n    \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001\\\": \\\"OPEN — top-level fields lock_branch etc. not dropped despite D-048 claim (CORR-MAJ-001)\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"24f20023-e5e9-4fd3-b33b-6e24125d8460\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.7432351000000001,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":17,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":186270,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":1454012,\"output_tokens\":40384,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":186270,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":6931,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":181280,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":12498,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":12498},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":2558,\"outputTokens\":30,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.002708,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":17,\"outputTokens\":40384,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":1454012,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":186270,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.7405271,\"contextWindow\":600000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"5dc4852a-a80e-4f92-99df-df460cd9f53c\"}\n\n=====\n{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":602966,\"duration_api_ms\":603679,\"num_turns\":16,\"result\":\"I now have all the information I need. Let me produce the findings report.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"lens\\\": \\\"safety_bypass\\\",\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"APPROVED_WITH_FINDINGS\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Four MAJ findings prevent fixpoint. (1) validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags() accepts any tag name matching the SHA — tag-name shape (vN.M.K) is never validated, so a non-release tag pushed to the SCP repo satisfies Gate 3 SHA validation. (2) GATE2_CAUTION_LINE is assembled with ${OPERATOR} at line 714, inside check_forward_mode_safety(), which runs before OPERATOR is set at line 1147 — the CAUTION log-block line records 'Operator @' with a blank username, breaking operator attribution in the load-bearing audit primitive. (3) D-048 explicitly claims --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification 'is only allowed when prior_restore_evidence_present returns true' — the code does not enforce this: when prior_restore_evidence_present() is false the flag is silently accepted, GATE2_CAUTION_LINE is never set, and no audit trace is produced. D-048 governance record is false. (4) TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-FILE-TOCTOU-001 is carried forward but not resolved: RESTORE_PRE_STATE is read twice from disk (cat line 870 vs validate_restore_source_json line 871); the canonical-context guard and all RESTORE_TARGET_* extractions use the raw cat read, not the validated payload — a file-swap between reads bypasses validation. Three MIN and one nit round out the surface. Set-equality verify phase, transform inclusion list, posture-degradation flag enumeration (all 7 present), and VERSIONING.md coverage (all 4 new flags listed) verified correct.\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SB-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Tag name shape is not validated — any tag name matching the SHA satisfies Gate 3 SHA validation, not just vN.M.K release tags.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags() (lines 590–654): matched_tag is set to ${ref#refs/tags/} for the first ref whose SHA matches. No check that matched_tag matches /^v[0-9]+\\\\\\\\.[0-9]+\\\\\\\\.[0-9]+$/. Both lightweight (commit) and annotated (tag-object) paths set matched_tag unconditionally on SHA equality.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"An operator or CI job that can push any tag to jrnb2024/standards-control-plane (e.g., a ci-probe or test-deploy tag) pointing to a known commit SHA could satisfy --expected-wrapper-sha Gate 3 validation for that SHA even if no vN.M.K release tag exists. Tag-protection rulesets (D-030/D-034) provide partial mitigation but are not enforced in the code path.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"After resolving matched_tag, validate it against a regex: if ! printf '%s' \\\\\\\"$matched_tag\\\\\\\" | grep -qE '^v[0-9]+\\\\\\\\.[0-9]+\\\\\\\\.[0-9]+$'; then echo 'error: matched tag is not a vN.M.K release tag' >&2; exit 2; fi. Also add a test asserting that a non-vN.M.K tag name is rejected even when its SHA matches.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SB-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"GATE2_CAUTION_LINE is assigned with ${OPERATOR} expanding to empty string — the load-bearing audit-log CAUTION line records 'Operator @' with blank username.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"OPERATOR=\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\" (line 117 initial declaration). GATE2_CAUTION_LINE=\\\\\\\"...Operator @${OPERATOR} acknowledges...\\\\\\\" assigned inside check_forward_mode_safety() at line 714. OPERATOR is not set to the real username until line 1147 (gh api user). The heredoc at lines 1193–1230 expands ${GATE2_CAUTION_LINE} as an already-fixed string — re-expansion of ${OPERATOR} does not occur. Lines 1169/1205 (main 'Operator:' header) ARE correct because they expand ${OPERATOR} at heredoc-emit time.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"The CAUTION line — identified by D-048 and ADOPT-001 §12.8 as the auditable bypass record — omits operator identity. An auditor reviewing the log block cannot determine who invoked the bypass from the CAUTION line itself (though the header does carry the name). Breaks the forensic completeness of the audit primitive.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Move GATE2_CAUTION_LINE assignment to after OPERATOR is set at line 1147, or use a lazy-expansion pattern: use a placeholder and construct the final line at heredoc-emit time using a format string rather than a pre-assigned variable with early ${OPERATOR} substitution.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SB-003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"D-048 falsely states --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification 'is only allowed when prior_restore_evidence_present returns true' — the code silently accepts the flag when prior_restore_evidence_present() is false, with no error and no audit trail.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"D-048 (line 102 of DECISIONS.md): 'the bypass is only allowed when prior_restore_evidence_present returns true'. Code: the if prior_restore_evidence_present block (line 707–721) is the only place ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION=1 has any effect. When the block is not entered (no prior evidence), the flag is accepted, GATE2_CAUTION_LINE stays \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\", no sleep fires, and no log-block caution is emitted. The top-level mutex checks (lines 298–306) block --expected-wrapper-sha combined with the flag but do not block the flag alone on cold-start.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"D-048 makes a false security assurance: auditors reading the governance record believe the flag is gated but it is not. A careless operator passing --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification on a fresh first-time enable gets no error and no audit trace; if prior_restore_evidence_present() is ever fooled (e.g., log-file tampering), the Gate 3 bypass produces zero audit signal.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add an explicit rejection early in check_forward_mode_safety(): if [ $ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION -eq 1 ] and prior_restore_evidence_present() is false, emit error 'prior restore evidence required for --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification' and exit 2. Then amend D-048 to accurately describe the enforcement. Add a test: cold-start repo + --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification → exit 2.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SB-004\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-FILE-TOCTOU-001 is unresolved: RESTORE_PRE_STATE is read twice from disk; a file-swap between reads can deliver a different payload to the canonical-context guard than what the validator accepted.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Line 870: RESTORE_TARGET_JSON=$(cat \\\\\\\"$RESTORE_PRE_STATE\\\\\\\"). Line 871: RESTORE_PAYLOAD=$(validate_restore_source_json \\\\\\\"$RESTORE_PRE_STATE\\\\\\\"). All RESTORE_TARGET_* variables (strict, contexts, admins, force-pushes, deletions) derive from RESTORE_TARGET_JSON (raw cat). The canonical-context guard at lines 946–963 uses RESTORE_TARGET_JSON. RESTORE_PAYLOAD (validated Python output) is used only for RESTORE_PUT_PAYLOAD and RESTORE_SIGNATURES_ENABLED. The carry-forward TF in DISPATCH-NOTE confirms this is a known open defect.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"A filesystem-level attacker (or a malicious operator) could serve a valid JSON to the Python validator on the second read while delivering a different JSON via the first cat read. The canonical-context guard and verify phase then operate against unvalidated content. Race window is narrow but the fix is trivial.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Read the file once into a variable: PRE_STATE_RAW=$(cat \\\\\\\"$RESTORE_PRE_STATE\\\\\\\"). Pass the content via stdin or env to validate_restore_source_json rather than the file path; have the function output the transformed payload from the same in-memory string. All subsequent uses of RESTORE_TARGET_JSON and RESTORE_PAYLOAD derive from the single read. Update validate_restore_source_json to accept stdin.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SB-005\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"--i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible is silently accepted (no error, no warning) when the wrapper IS readable, making the flag interface misleading with no posture downgrade.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Lines 740–762: the ACK_WRAPPER_INACCESSIBLE check appears only in the else branch (when wrapper_content is empty). When wrapper_content is non-empty, the if branch performs the verification and ACK_WRAPPER_INACCESSIBLE is never consulted. The top-level mutex only rejects it in --restore mode (lines 292–295). No guard rejects the flag in forward mode when wrapper is readable.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"An operator who passes the flag 'just in case' while the wrapper is readable sees no feedback. Verification still runs (no downgrade), but the operator cannot confirm which code path was taken. Under a social-engineering scenario, an attacker instructing an operator to 'add --i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible' might create false confidence that verification was bypassed.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"After wrapper verification succeeds (line 742 log), check if ACK_WRAPPER_INACCESSIBLE=1 and emit a warning: 'WARNING: --i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible passed but wrapper is readable; verification was performed normally. Remove the flag to suppress this warning.' This closes the silent-acceptance surface without changing security posture.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SB-006\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"RESTORE_PRE_STATE path is not realpath-resolved before file opens — symlink following is unrestricted at both the Python open() and the cat call.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"validate_restore_source_json opens sys.argv[1] via open(path) without os.path.realpath(). cat \\\\\\\"$RESTORE_PRE_STATE\\\\\\\" also follows symlinks. check-invocation-log-entry.sh uses resolve_inside_repo_root() / python3 os.path.realpath() for all its file paths (lines 130–143). No equivalent guard exists in enable-required-check.sh for RESTORE_PRE_STATE.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"A symlink at the RESTORE_PRE_STATE path that is swapped to point outside the repo root (or to a sensitive file) could be consumed without operator awareness. Combined with the TOCTOU issue in SB-004, a symlink swap during the read gap yields unvalidated content. Risk is low (requires local filesystem write access) but the defense is absent.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Resolve the path before use: RESTORE_PRE_STATE=$(python3 -c 'import os,sys; print(os.path.realpath(sys.argv[1]))' \\\\\\\"$RESTORE_PRE_STATE\\\\\\\"). Optionally assert the resolved path is under a known safe directory (e.g., the REPO_ROOT or CWD).\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SB-007\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Wrapper grep uses line-by-line filtering that is not YAML-aware — multi-line YAML block scalars or anchor-alias patterns could diverge between grep-match and GitHub Actions runtime execution.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Line 741: grep -vE '^[[:space:]]*#' | grep -qE '^[[:space:]]*uses:[[:space:]]+[^#]*standards-control-plane[^#]*@SHA'. This strips comment lines and matches a uses: line. GitHub Actions YAML parser handles anchors, aliases, and folded/literal block scalars; grep does not. A crafted wrapper with a YAML anchor pointing the uses: value to a different string would pass grep (anchored line matches) while executing differently at runtime.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"In practice limited: GitHub Actions requires uses: to be a simple scalar string; block scalars and anchors are not supported for the uses: field. However, the grep approach cannot provide a formal guarantee of match-to-execution equivalence. Classification: defense correctness gap, not an active bypass path.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a note in ADOPT-001 §12.8 and the script's inline comment that the grep approach is heuristic; a future hardening step could fetch the raw YAML, parse it with python3's yaml.safe_load(), and extract .jobs.*.steps[].uses directly. For now, the practical risk is negligible given GitHub Actions' strict scalar constraint on uses:.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SB-nit-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags() hardcodes 'repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/git/refs/tags' — the trailing hyphen and literal org/repo are brittle.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Lines 593 and 638 use the literal string jrnb2024/standards-control-plane (note trailing hyphen). If this is the actual repo name it is fragile to rename; if it is a typo for standards-control-plane the function will always fail (no tags found → exit 2). The REPO_ROOT variable is available but not used to derive the remote URL.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"If the trailing hyphen is a typo, Gate 3 SHA validation always fails silently (exit 2 with 'SHA not found'), forcing operators to use --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification every time. Correctness hazard, not a security bypass.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Derive the SCP repo identifier from git remote get-url origin or a top-level constant (SCP_REPO_SLUG). Verify the trailing hyphen is intentional or correct it. Add a test fixture that exercises the function against a known fake-tags response to catch URL regressions.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"e04f23e1-6099-42a7-854c-c0aabecb3e21\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.12453695,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":10,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":122335,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":522039,\"output_tokens\":33782,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":122335,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":5889,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":125886,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":3957,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":3957},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":2264,\"outputTokens\":29,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.002409,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":10,\"outputTokens\":33782,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":522039,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":122335,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.1221279499999999,\"contextWindow\":600000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"6686d04c-9ffe-4fcd-b639-f81a5ea2d516\"}\n\n=====\n{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":357578,\"duration_api_ms\":358245,\"num_turns\":23,\"result\":\"Now I have sufficient data to produce the structured review. Emitting the JSON findings.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"reviewer_id\\\": \\\"sonnet-r1-completeness-governance\\\",\\n  \\\"lens\\\": \\\"completeness_governance\\\",\\n  \\\"slice_id\\\": \\\"WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2\\\",\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"APPROVED_WITH_FINDINGS\\\",\\n  \\\"criterion\\\": \\\"(b): ≤2 MAJ + 0 CRIT on this complete review cycle\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The 024B-extras-2 depth-defense surface is substantively complete. All 10 Scope (in) ACs map to concrete deliverables: --expected-wrapper-sha + validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags() with annotated-tag dereferencing (script:590-654), --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification with conditional CAUTION/sleep gated on prior_restore_evidence_present (script:707-720), --i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible (script:749-755), canonical-context guard (script:947-964), set-equality verify phase replacing grep -F (script:1095), transform inclusion lists ALLOWED_*_KEYS (script:440-449/469-510), mutex checks (script:280-303), ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 3 rewritten with automated --expected-wrapper-sha procedure and Post-break-glass permanence callout (ADOPT-001:1265), D-048 filed at DECISIONS.md row 102 with 7-component contract citing SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11 and bus-factor-1, VERSIONING.md lists all 17 protected flags including all 6 posture-degradation flags. D-048 reservation note converted to 'consumed and filed'. No silent descope; no extras-3 waterfall. Three MAJ governance gaps: STATUS.md TF closure state stale for two delivered TFs; workflow guard inline simulation missing 024B-extras-2 in its tooling-slice enum; ADOPT-001 §12.8 reference line omits D-048. One MIN: STATUS.md header date not updated. Eight of 10 carry-forward TFs correctly tracked as open for future slices; two implemented TFs (SET-EQ-001, TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001) not marked closed.\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-MAJ-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"STATUS.md TF entries for TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001 and TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ-001 remain marked '(open)' despite both being implemented in this slice and ratified by D-048.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"STATUS.md lines 346+352 show both TFs as '(open)'. DISPATCH-NOTE TF table states 'TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001 (this one IS closed by the slice's transform inclusion list)'. D-048 rationale: 'transform inclusion lists close the lock_branch / required_linear_history / block_creations posture gap (per R30 SAFE-MAJ-001)'. Set-equality verify IS at script:1095; ALLOWED_*_KEYS constants ARE at script:440-449.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Audit-trail inconsistency. Governance reviewers, future Codex dispatches, or 024C kickoff ceremony reading STATUS.md TF list would not know these TFs are closed, potentially re-opening resolved work or failing TF-count closure checks.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Update STATUS.md TF entries for TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001 and TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ-001 from '(open)' to '(closed: implemented in 024B-extras-2)'. Add closure date and reference to D-048 for each.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-MAJ-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Workflow guard inline simulation in test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh (run_workflow_guard_case, line ~207) has stale tooling-slice case statement missing '024B-extras-2'; STATUS.md claim of '2 test sites updated' is therefore inaccurate.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh line ~207: 'case \\\\\\\"$slice_id\\\\\\\" in\\\\\\\\n  024A|024B-core|024B-extras|024G)' — missing 024B-extras-2. Actual workflow file check-invocation-log-entry.yml line 68: '024A|024B-core|024B-extras|024B-extras-2|024G' — correctly includes it. STATUS.md step 2 (2026-05-13): 'Tooling-slice enum updated to include 024B-extras-2 at 2 test sites'. The inline simulation is a third site missed.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"If a workflow guard test case is added for 024B-extras-2, it will produce enforce=true instead of enforce=false, causing a test failure. More immediately, STATUS.md's coverage claim is inaccurate, masking the test gap from future fix-round reviewers.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Update the run_workflow_guard_case inline case statement at line ~207 to '024A|024B-core|024B-extras|024B-extras-2|024G'. Add a workflow guard test case verifying that a DISPATCH-NOTE with slice_id=024B-extras-2 produces enforce=false in GITHUB_OUTPUT. Correct STATUS.md step 2 to '3 test sites'.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-MAJ-003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"ADOPT-001 §12.8 reference line (line 1280) cites D-047, D-035, D-030 but omits D-048, leaving the automated Gate 3 governance record unreferenced from the procedure it governs.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"ADOPT-001 line 1280: 'Reference: D-047, WP-SCP-024 invariant 7, D-035, D-030, and the break-glass guidance in docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md.' D-048 is the ratifying decision for --expected-wrapper-sha automated Gate 3 and the permanence callout at ADOPT-001:1265. D-047's rationale explicitly says Gate 2 automated verification is absent from extras-1 and deferred to D-048.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"An operator consulting §12.8 to understand the trust-model basis for automated Gate 3 verification is not directed to D-048, the canonical governance record. Also inconsistent: the permanence callout (ADOPT-001:1265) is a D-048 contribution but D-047 is cited as the authority.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Update ADOPT-001 §12.8 reference line to: 'Reference: D-047 (core restore contract), D-048 (automated Gate 3 + permanence), WP-SCP-024 invariant 7, D-035, D-030, and the break-glass guidance in docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md.'\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-MIN-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"STATUS.md header 'Last updated: 2026-05-12' was not updated to 2026-05-13 when the 2026-05-13 chain entry was appended.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"STATUS.md line 2: '**Last updated:** 2026-05-12 (WP-SCP-024 024B-extras fix-round-31...)'. STATUS.md contains a '## Today's chain (2026-05-13 — 024B-extras-2 depth-defense surface)' section with 4 steps including D-048 filing.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Minor audit-trail confusion: the document's declared currency date is one day stale, causing the chain entry date and the header date to mismatch. Low risk but inconsistent with the standard STATUS.md maintenance procedure applied in all prior chains.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Update STATUS.md header to: '**Last updated:** 2026-05-13 (WP-SCP-024 024B-extras-2 depth-defense surface; D-048 filed)'.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-nit-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"check-invocation-log-entry.yml was modified to add '024B-extras-2' to the tooling-slice short-circuit case (line 68), but this change was not listed in the DISPATCH-NOTE opening checklist.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Workflow file line 68: '024A|024B-core|024B-extras|024B-extras-2|024G'. DISPATCH-NOTE opening checklist (lines 120-129) does not mention the workflow file modification. The modification is correct and necessary (without it the CI would enforce invocation-log checks on this slice's own PR). But it is undocumented.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Negligible operational impact since the modification is correct. Creates a minor discrepancy between the checklist and the actual scope — a governance-trace artifact for future slice authors referencing this slice as a pattern.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a note to the DISPATCH-NOTE opening checklist acknowledging the workflow tooling-slice enum update, or add a note to STATUS.md step 2 specifically calling out the workflow file as a 3rd site alongside the 2 already mentioned.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"d7682bb9-b6cb-4d92-8cd1-de011dab745e\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.14107335,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":11,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":148695,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":761667,\"output_tokens\":23477,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":148695,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":13009,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":133810,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":22393,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":22393},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":2634,\"outputTokens\":29,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.0027790000000000002,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":11,\"outputTokens\":23477,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":761667,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":148695,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.1382943500000002,\"contextWindow\":600000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"ec7614a6-f277-467b-b9d8-6de611240788\"}\n\n=====\n# DISPATCH-NOTE — WP-SCP-024 slice 024B-extras-2 (depth-defense surface) — SKELETON\n\n**Date:** 2026-05-12\n**Branch:** `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-2-v2` (off origin/main at `d7b16d0`, branched fresh post-extras-1-merge). The original `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-2` branch at fd62641 preserves pre-carve R7-R16 work as audit-trail reference.\n**Predecessor:** WP-SCP-024 024B-extras-1 merged at `d7b16d0` on 2026-05-12 (PR #113).\n**Decision filed:** D-048 (depth-defense surface ratification).\n\n`cascade-status: not applicable` — this slice ships depth-defense additions; not a cohort cascade slice.\n`slice-type: tooling`\n\n## Backstory\n\nWP-SCP-024 024B-extras was operator-decided split on 2026-05-11 (`docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md`) after 16 R-cycles + 38 hours of session wall-time without reaching criterion (b) fixpoint. The R-trajectory plateaued at ~5 MAJ per round (R12 4 / R13 4 / R14 3 / R15 8 / R16 6) with most findings being latent depth-defects in the depth-defense surface, not just-added-code regressions.\n\nThe depth-defense surface was extracted into this slice (024B-extras-2). The core --restore + ADOPT-001 §12.8 (manual Gate 3) + workflow CI gate shipped in 024B-extras-1 — that's what 024C cascade needs. This slice adds the automated Gate 3 verification + canonical-context guard + set-equality verify phase + transform inclusion-list defense + annotated-tag dereferencing.\n\nThis branch (`feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-2`) was created at the 024B-extras carve point (fd62641, post-fix-round-16) so all R7-R16 work is preserved. Re-applying it on top of merged 024B-extras-1 needs a rebase or cherry-pick of the depth-defense diff.\n\n## Why\n\nThe depth-defense surface is real defensive value:\n1. **Gate 3 wrapper-pin verification** prevents an operator from re-enabling required-check after a break-glass cycle when the adopter wrapper file is still pinned to a broken SHA. Manual procedure (in 024B-extras-1 §12.8) is human-error-prone; automating it adds a real safety property.\n2. **Canonical-context guard** (`--i-understand-restore-replaces-required-check-context`) prevents an attacker-modified pre-state JSON from silently replacing the policy gate with attacker-controlled context. Real safety property.\n3. **Set-equality verify phase** prevents spurious FAIL=1 + exit 1 on legitimate restore when GitHub returns contexts in a different order than the pre-state JSON. Real reliability property.\n4. **Transform inclusion list** prevents unknown nested fields from passing through to PUT body. Defense-in-depth.\n5. **Annotated-tag dereferencing** enables Gate 3 SHA validation regardless of whether SCP-self uses lightweight or annotated tags.\n\nThese are all valuable. They just don't gate 024C cascade onboarding — invariant 7's <30-min rollback SLO is satisfied by the core --restore mode in 024B-extras-1.\n\n## Scope (in)\n\n| Deliverable | Path | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `--expected-wrapper-sha SHA` flag + `validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags()` | `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` | Re-add the function with annotated-tag dereferencing (gh api git/refs/tags/* via --paginate + per-annotated-tag git/tags/<sha> dereference). Validates supplied SHA against release-tag SHAs. |\n| `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` flag + conditional CAUTION/sleep | `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` | Re-add ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION + GATE2_CAUTION_LINE. CAUTION + 5s sleep fires ONLY when prior_restore_evidence_present (R16-CORR-002 closure). |\n| `--i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible` flag + wrapper-pin verification | `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` | Re-add ACK_WRAPPER_INACCESSIBLE + WRAPPER_INACCESSIBLE_CAUTION_LINE + gh api contents grep-anchored uses: match. |\n| `--i-understand-restore-replaces-required-check-context` flag + canonical-context guard | `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` | Re-add ACK_RESTORE_REPLACES_REQUIRED_CHECK_CONTEXT + jq element-wise canonical-context check. |\n| Set-equality verify phase | `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` | Replace comma-substring grep -F with jq `--argjson expected_contexts ... sort == sort` comparison. |\n| Transform inclusion list | `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` | Add ALLOWED_REQUIRED_STATUS_CHECKS_KEYS / ALLOWED_REQUIRED_PR_REVIEWS_KEYS / ALLOWED_RESTRICTIONS_KEYS to transform(). |\n| ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 3 update | `docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md` | Replace the manual Gate 3 from 024B-extras-1 with automated --expected-wrapper-sha procedure. Re-add Post-break-glass permanence callout. |\n| D-048 row | `docs/DECISIONS.md` | Ratify depth-defense surface. Includes trust-model: Gate 3 SHA-pin is mandatory + permanence applies post-break-glass. |\n| All extracted tests | `tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh` | Re-add tests for: tag validation, wrapper-pin verification, canonical-context guard, set-equality verify, transform inclusion list, mutex tests, annotated-tag dereference. |\n| Mutex checks | `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` | --restore + --expected-wrapper-sha + --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification + --i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible incompatibilities. |\n| 6th posture-degradation flag in VERSIONING.md + branch-protection helper list | `policies/VERSIONING.md` | Re-add --i-understand-restore-replaces-required-check-context + other 3 flags. |\n\n## Scope (out)\n\n- 024C PIM cascade onboarding (unblocked when 024B-extras-1 merges).\n- TF-023E-002 closure.\n- D-021 May-31 atomic-workday filing.\n\n## Recovery path — Rebase or cherry-pick from fd62641\n\nAfter 024B-extras-1 merges, this branch contains the full pre-carve state. Choose one:\n\n### Option A — Rebase 024B-extras-2 onto merged 024B-extras-1\n```bash\ngit fetch origin\ngit checkout feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-2\ngit rebase origin/main  # may have conflicts; resolve preferring 024B-extras-2's depth-defense additions\n```\nThis preserves the full R-cycle history but rebuilds the commit chain over the merged 024B-extras-1.\n\n### Option B — Cherry-pick depth-defense diff onto a fresh branch\n```bash\ngit fetch origin\ngit checkout -b feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-2-v2 origin/main\n# Manually re-apply the depth-defense additions from feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-2 vs 024B-extras-1-merge-point\ngit diff <024B-extras-1-merge-SHA> feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-2 -- scripts/ tests/ docs/adoption/ docs/DECISIONS.md docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/ policies/ > /tmp/depth-defense.diff\ngit apply /tmp/depth-defense.diff\n# Stage + commit as one clean \"024B-extras-2 depth-defense surface\" commit\n```\nThis produces a clean single-commit slice without 16 rounds of fix-round commit churn.\n\n**Recommendation: Option B.** The R-cycle commit history is preserved in the `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-2` branch tip; the rebase-vs-cherry-pick choice is about what gets reviewed in the PR. A single-commit slice is cleaner for the new R-cycle.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] All extracted features re-implemented and tests passing\n- [ ] D-048 filed\n- [ ] ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 3 automated procedure\n- [ ] STATUS.md chain entry\n- [ ] 3-lens R1+R2 fixpoint (≤2 MAJ + 0 CRIT per criterion (b))\n- [ ] CI green\n- [ ] Self-merge per D-040\n\n## Sequencing\n\n| Phase | Work | Mode | Wall |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | Pre-flight: 024B-extras-1 merged + this branch rebased/cherry-picked | Operator | ~30 min |\n| 1 | Single Codex pass to re-apply the depth-defense diff (already authored) | Codex T3 | ~15 min |\n| 2 | 3× sequential Sonnet R1 review | Sonnet | ~30 min |\n| 3 | Fix-rounds (expected 1-2 given smaller surface + carried-forward R16 fixes) | Codex + Sonnet | ~1-2 hrs |\n| 4 | Final R-fixpoint + self-merge | Opus | ~10 min |\n\nTarget: 024B-extras-2 merged within ~4-5 hours wall-clock (smaller surface; R16's depth-finds already addressed).\n\n## Reservation guard\n\nD-048 reserved for this slice. Codex must NOT assign D-048 to anything else.\n\n---\n\n**Status:** ACTIVE — opened 2026-05-12 post-extras-1-merge. 10 carry-forward TFs from extras-1 to absorb:\n\n| TF | Source | Class |\n|---|---|---|\n| TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ-001 | extras-1 SCOPE-CORRECTION-2 carve + R20/R22/R25/R27/R29/R30 cross-lens | restore-mode set-equality verify |\n| TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-PATH-CONTAINMENT-001 | extras-1 fix-round-20 | `--restore` path containment guard |\n| TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-COHORT-REGEX-MULTICHAR-001 | extras-1 fix-round-20 | cohort regex multi-char support |\n| TF-024B-STEP7-FIXTURE-SEQ-001 | extras-1 fix-round-20 | step-7 fixture alignment polish |\n| TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-STAGED-RESTORE-TEST-001 | extras-1 fix-round-20 | staged-but-uncommitted prior-restore test |\n| TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-FILE-TOCTOU-001 | extras-1 fix-round-21 | RESTORE_PRE_STATE TOCTOU hardening |\n| TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-WORKFLOW-PIN-BASE-BRANCH-001 | extras-1 fix-round-21 | CI workflow pin to base-branch script |\n| TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-POLICY-CHECK-TARGET-FILTER-TESTS-001 | extras-1 fix-round-24 | per-test coverage for path-based excludes |\n| TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-PUT-BODY-SHAPE-ASSERTIONS-001 | extras-1 fix-round-25 | extend PUT-body shape assertions across all restore tests |\n| TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001 | extras-1 fix-round-31 (R30 SAFE-MAJ-001) | transform inclusion-list (replaces exclusion-list); covers lock_branch / required_linear_history / block_creations posture gap |\n\n## Slice opening checklist\n\n- [x] DISPATCH-NOTE drafted (this file)\n- [x] Branch `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-2-v2` opened off main `d7b16d0`\n- [ ] Codex dispatch to apply depth-defense diff (extracted from preserved branch `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-2` at fd62641 OR re-implemented from this DISPATCH-NOTE)\n- [ ] 3-lens R1 review on initial implementation\n- [ ] Fix-rounds to fixpoint\n- [ ] PR + self-merge per D-040\n\nThis slice does NOT gate 024C. The cohort cascade can open in parallel once FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closes (ACC-side).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n \\\"(transform\\\\(|validate_restore_source_json|check_forward_mode_safety|validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags|GATE2_CAUTION_LINE|WRAPPER_INACCESSIBLE_CAUTION_LINE|RESTORE_PRE_STATE|OPERATOR|prior_restore_evidence_present|ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION|CAUTION|slice_id|024B-extras-2|required_status_checks|set\\\\(value.keys\\\\(\\\\)\\\\) == \\\\{\\\\\\\"enabled\\\\\\\"\\\\})\\\" scripts/enable-required-check.sh tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh STATUS.md docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md docs/DECISIONS.md policies/VERSIONING.md docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/DISPATCH-NOTE.md docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/r1-correctness.json docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/r1-safety_bypass.json docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/r1-completeness_governance.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n \\\"(transform\\\\(|validate_restore_source_json|check_forward_mode_safety|validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags|GATE2_CAUTION_LINE|WRAPPER_INACCESSIBLE_CAUTION_LINE|RESTORE_PRE_STATE|OPERATOR|prior_restore_evidence_present|ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION|CAUTION|slice_id|024B-extras-2|required_status_checks|set\\\\(value.keys\\\\(\\\\)\\\\) == \\\\{\\\\\\\"enabled\\\\\\\"\\\\})\\\" scripts/enable-required-check.sh tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh STATUS.md docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md docs/DECISIONS.md policies/VERSIONING.md docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/DISPATCH-NOTE.md docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/r1-correctness.json docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/r1-safety_bypass.json docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/r1-completeness_governance.json\"","aggregated_output":"docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/r1-correctness.json:1:{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":618690,\"duration_api_ms\":619500,\"num_turns\":27,\"result\":\"Now I have a thorough understanding of the codebase. Let me produce the structured findings report.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"slice\\\": \\\"WP-SCP-024 024B-extras-2\\\",\\n  \\\"lens\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\\n  \\\"reviewer\\\": \\\"sonnet-r1-correctness\\\",\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"CHANGES_REQUIRED\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Depth-defense surface is largely sound: Gate 3 flow, wrapper-pin verification, canonical-context guard, annotated-tag dereference, and mutex checks are all correctly implemented. Set-equality verify uses RESTORE_TARGET_JSON as source-of-truth (correct). ACK flag routing is correct. Six correctness gaps found: (1) the transform inclusion lists close nested-field leakage for required_status_checks/reviews/restrictions but leave top-level fields (lock_branch, required_linear_history, block_creations) passing through as truthy booleans — D-048's stated coverage claim does not hold for these fields. (2) RESTORE_PRE_STATE path has no traversal guard unlike --repo/--branch. (3) CAUTION log line hardcodes the wrong ACK flag name when ACK_RESTORE_REPLACES_REQUIRED_CHECK_CONTEXT is used for the empty-contexts case, producing a false audit entry. (4) Workflow guard test harness inline script missing 024B-extras-2 from tooling case; production workflow is correct but the test provides no coverage for 024B-extras-2 dispatch-note short-circuit. (5) No context-order-shuffled test per TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ-001. (6) No test for --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification without prior restore evidence despite DISPATCH-NOTE claiming this case is covered and D-048 stating the bypass is only permitted with prior evidence present.\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-MAJ-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"transform() does not drop lock_branch/required_linear_history/block_creations from PUT body; D-048 claims inclusion lists close this gap but they only apply to nested keys within required_status_checks, required_pull_request_reviews, and restrictions.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh lines 476-477: the generic elif branch converts any {enabled: bool} dict to a boolean, so a pre-state JSON with lock_branch:{enabled:true} produces lock_branch:true in RESTORE_PUT_PAYLOAD. No top-level inclusion/exclusion list guards these fields. D-048 rationale: 'inclusion lists close the lock_branch / required_linear_history / block_creations posture gap'. TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Attacker-modified pre-state JSON (requiring CODEOWNERS-protected file modification) with lock_branch:{enabled:true} would lock the branch as a side-effect of restore. D-048's claimed fix is incomplete for top-level {enabled:bool} fields.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add explicit exclusion of lock_branch, required_linear_history, block_creations in the transform() function's top-level key loop, or add a top-level inclusion list for only the documented restore PUT fields.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-MAJ-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"--restore path argument has no path-traversal or containment validation, unlike --repo and --branch which have dedicated guards.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh lines 226-231: RESTORE_PRE_STATE=$2 with no validation. Lines 344-360: --repo and --branch have leading-dot and '..' guards. RESTORE_PRE_STATE is passed to cat and Python open() at lines 870-871 with no sanitization. TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-PATH-CONTAINMENT-001.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"An operator could accidentally pass a path outside the working directory (e.g. --restore ../../secrets.json). While the validator would reject non-JSON files, the attack surface is inconsistent with the security posture applied to other path arguments.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a path containment check on RESTORE_PRE_STATE: resolve realpath and assert it is readable and within acceptable bounds, consistent with the --repo/--branch guards.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-MAJ-003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"When ACK_RESTORE_REPLACES_REQUIRED_CHECK_CONTEXT satisfies the restore_contexts==0 (empty contexts) check, the CAUTION log entry hardcodes 'acknowledged via --i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks', producing a false audit trail.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh lines 951-957: the empty-contexts branch allows either ACK_RESTORE_REQUIRED_CHECKS_REMOVAL or ACK_RESTORE_REPLACES_REQUIRED_CHECK_CONTEXT. But line 957 always emits CAUTION text citing --i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks regardless of which flag was used. The log-sanitization test at line 2458 passes --i-understand-restore-replaces-required-check-context and would produce this false entry.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Invocation log records incorrect operator acknowledgement flag. Audit trail misleads post-incident review: log says operator acknowledged via flag X when operator actually used flag Y.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Condition the CAUTION message on which flag was set: if ACK_RESTORE_REQUIRED_CHECKS_REMOVAL emit the removes-required-checks message; if ACK_RESTORE_REPLACES_REQUIRED_CHECK_CONTEXT emit the replaces-context message.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-MAJ-004\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Workflow guard test harness (run_workflow_guard_case inline script, line ~206) is missing 024B-extras-2 from the tooling-slice case list; production workflow is correct but no test verifies 024B-extras-2 short-circuit path.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"test file line ~206: case $slice_id in 024A|024B-core|024B-extras|024G) — 024B-extras-2 absent. Production .github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml lines 67-76: 024A|024B-core|024B-extras|024B-extras-2|024G correctly present. No run_workflow_guard_case test exercises a 024B-extras-2 DISPATCH-NOTE path. TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-WORKFLOW-PIN-BASE-BRANCH-001.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"A PR touching docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/DISPATCH-NOTE.md would be incorrectly treated as cohort by the test harness, masking any regression where production workflow short-circuit fails. TF not addressed.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add 024B-extras-2 to the inline script's case list and add a run_workflow_guard_case test that sends a 024B-extras-2 DISPATCH-NOTE path and asserts enforce=false + Tooling slice message.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-MAJ-005\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"No context-order-shuffled test for set-equality verify phase; TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ-001 explicitly requires this test case and DISPATCH-NOTE lists restore-set-equality(context-order-shuffled) as covered.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Searched test file for shuffled/set-equality/context-order test: not found. Existing tests (restore-checks-canonical-plus-extra, restore-checks-canonical) have AFTER contexts in identical order to pre-state. The jq sort==sort at script line 1094-1099 is logically correct but the shuffled-order path is untested. DISPATCH-NOTE scope claims this test exists.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Contract between DISPATCH-NOTE claimed coverage and actual test coverage is broken. If a regression introduced order-sensitive comparison, the shuffle case would silently fail in production.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a restore test case where pre-state contexts are [context-a, context-b] and after.json returns [context-b, context-a]; assert verification passes.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-MAJ-006\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification is silently accepted as a no-op when no prior restore evidence is present; D-048 states the bypass is only allowed when prior_restore_evidence_present returns true, and DISPATCH-NOTE claims a no-prior-evidence test exists.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh check_forward_mode_safety(): ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION is checked only inside the if prior_restore_evidence_present block (lines 707-721). Without prior evidence, the flag produces no CAUTION, no sleep, no error. No test in test file exercises this path. D-048: 'bypass is only allowed when prior_restore_evidence_present returns true'. DISPATCH-NOTE: 'enable-no-gate-2-verification (mutex, no-prior-evidence)'.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"A cold-start operator who mistakenly passes --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification receives no feedback that the flag is inappropriate; declarative D-048 constraint is unenforceable. Missing test per DISPATCH-NOTE scope.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add an explicit rejection (exit 2) when ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION=1 but prior_restore_evidence_present returns false, and add a test asserting this exit 2.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-MIN-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-STAGED-RESTORE-TEST-001 not addressed: no explicit test for staged (git-added but uncommitted) prior-restore evidence detection.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Test enable-working-tree-prior-restore (line 4310) modifies the log file in the working tree without git-add; no test stages with git add before running. prior_restore_evidence_present() uses git diff HEAD which covers staged changes, but this behavior is untested.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Low risk — git diff HEAD semantically covers staged changes — but the TF contract is not satisfied. A future refactor that switches to git diff (unstaged only) would silently miss staged evidence.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a test that does git add on the modified log before invoking enable-required-check.sh without --expected-wrapper-sha, asserting exit 2 with prior --restore evidence detected.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-MIN-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-PUT-BODY-SHAPE-ASSERTIONS-001 not addressed: PUT body jq assertions present only in force-pushes, deletions, and null-status-checks tests; canonical-context, wrong-context-ack, and log-sanitization tests do not assert PUT body contents.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Tests restore-checks-canonical (line 3015), restore-log-sanitization (line 2458), restore-checks-embedded-comma (line 2917) check exit code and stdout but do not assert put-body.json contents. TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-PUT-BODY-SHAPE-ASSERTIONS-001 explicitly tracks this gap.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"A transform regression that corrupts the PUT body shape would not be caught by the context-guard tests, which only verify CAUTION emission and exit codes.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add jq assertions on $fake_gh_dir/put-body.json in restore-checks-canonical, restore-checks-wrong-context-ack, and restore-checks-embedded-comma tests to assert the full required_status_checks shape.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-MIN-003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-POLICY-CHECK-TARGET-FILTER-TESTS-001 not addressed: workflow path filter (docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[C-Z]*/**) behavior untested for boundary slice IDs.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"check-invocation-log-entry.yml paths trigger on 024[C-Z]*/** but workflow guard tests only test 024B-extras and 024C. Slices like 024G (tooling) and edge cases for pattern matching are not covered. No test verifies that a 024B-extras-2 path triggers the workflow at all.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Workflow path filter correctness for 024G and any future alphabetically-later tooling slice is unverified.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add run_workflow_guard_case test for 024G DISPATCH-NOTE path to verify tooling short-circuit and for 024D/024E/024F to verify cohort enforcement path.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-nit-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Forward-mode log block emits two blank lines when both GATE2_CAUTION_LINE and WRAPPER_INACCESSIBLE_CAUTION_LINE are empty, between - **Plan-only:** no and - **PUT payload applied:**.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh lines 1210-1211: ${GATE2_CAUTION_LINE} and ${WRAPPER_INACCESSIBLE_CAUTION_LINE} on separate lines in the heredoc; when both are empty strings, two empty lines appear in the markdown log block output.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Cosmetic: emitted log block has inconsistent blank-line count depending on flag usage, which may confuse operators comparing log entries.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Guard each line: only emit when non-empty, e.g. [ -n \\\\\\\"$GATE2_CAUTION_LINE\\\\\\\" ] && printf '%s\\\\\\\\n' \\\\\\\"$GATE2_CAUTION_LINE\\\\\\\".\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CORR-nit-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Annotated-tag dereference only handles one level of indirection; a tag object pointing to another tag object (doubly-annotated) will not resolve to the commit SHA.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"enable-required-check.sh lines 638-644: gh api git/tags/<sha> --jq .object.sha returns the sha the tag points to. For a doubly-annotated tag, .object.sha is the inner tag sha, not the commit. The comparison if [ \\\\\\\"$annotated_commit_sha\\\\\\\" = \\\\\\\"$expected_sha\\\\\\\" ] then fails. SCP release tags are unlikely to be doubly-annotated but the limitation is undocumented.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"If SCP ever uses doubly-annotated tags for releases, --expected-wrapper-sha would fail to validate them even when the SHA is a valid release.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Document the single-level dereference limitation in the function header comment, or add a recursive follow for obj_type == 'tag'.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"carry_forward_tf_status\\\": {\\n    \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ-001\\\": \\\"OPEN — set-equality jq logic is correct but context-order-shuffled test missing (CORR-MAJ-005)\\\",\\n    \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-PATH-CONTAINMENT-001\\\": \\\"OPEN — no path containment guard on RESTORE_PRE_STATE (CORR-MAJ-002)\\\",\\n    \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-COHORT-REGEX-MULTICHAR-001\\\": \\\"CLOSED — workflow grep regex 024[A-Za-z][^/]* correctly matches 024B-extras-2; --tooling-slice-id enum includes 024B-extras-2\\\",\\n    \\\"TF-024B-STEP7-FIXTURE-SEQ-001\\\": \\\"OUT-OF-SCOPE for this slice (tooling only, no step-7 demo in 024B-extras-2)\\\",\\n    \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-STAGED-RESTORE-TEST-001\\\": \\\"OPEN — no staged-evidence test (CORR-MIN-001)\\\",\\n    \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-FILE-TOCTOU-001\\\": \\\"OPEN — RESTORE_PRE_STATE opened twice without hardening; low exploitability given bootstrap-only context; not flagged as MAJ\\\",\\n    \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-WORKFLOW-PIN-BASE-BRANCH-001\\\": \\\"OPEN — test harness inline script missing 024B-extras-2 (CORR-MAJ-004)\\\",\\n    \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-POLICY-CHECK-TARGET-FILTER-TESTS-001\\\": \\\"OPEN — boundary path filter tests missing (CORR-MIN-003)\\\",\\n    \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-PUT-BODY-SHAPE-ASSERTIONS-001\\\": \\\"OPEN — PUT body assertions absent in most restore tests (CORR-MIN-002)\\\",\\n    \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001\\\": \\\"OPEN — top-level fields lock_branch etc. not dropped despite D-048 claim (CORR-MAJ-001)\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"24f20023-e5e9-4fd3-b33b-6e24125d8460\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.7432351000000001,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":17,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":186270,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":1454012,\"output_tokens\":40384,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":186270,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":6931,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":181280,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":12498,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":12498},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":2558,\"outputTokens\":30,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.002708,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":17,\"outputTokens\":40384,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":1454012,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":186270,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.7405271,\"contextWindow\":600000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"5dc4852a-a80e-4f92-99df-df460cd9f53c\"}\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/r1-completeness_governance.json:1:{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":357578,\"duration_api_ms\":358245,\"num_turns\":23,\"result\":\"Now I have sufficient data to produce the structured review. Emitting the JSON findings.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"reviewer_id\\\": \\\"sonnet-r1-completeness-governance\\\",\\n  \\\"lens\\\": \\\"completeness_governance\\\",\\n  \\\"slice_id\\\": \\\"WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2\\\",\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"APPROVED_WITH_FINDINGS\\\",\\n  \\\"criterion\\\": \\\"(b): ≤2 MAJ + 0 CRIT on this complete review cycle\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"The 024B-extras-2 depth-defense surface is substantively complete. All 10 Scope (in) ACs map to concrete deliverables: --expected-wrapper-sha + validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags() with annotated-tag dereferencing (script:590-654), --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification with conditional CAUTION/sleep gated on prior_restore_evidence_present (script:707-720), --i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible (script:749-755), canonical-context guard (script:947-964), set-equality verify phase replacing grep -F (script:1095), transform inclusion lists ALLOWED_*_KEYS (script:440-449/469-510), mutex checks (script:280-303), ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 3 rewritten with automated --expected-wrapper-sha procedure and Post-break-glass permanence callout (ADOPT-001:1265), D-048 filed at DECISIONS.md row 102 with 7-component contract citing SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11 and bus-factor-1, VERSIONING.md lists all 17 protected flags including all 6 posture-degradation flags. D-048 reservation note converted to 'consumed and filed'. No silent descope; no extras-3 waterfall. Three MAJ governance gaps: STATUS.md TF closure state stale for two delivered TFs; workflow guard inline simulation missing 024B-extras-2 in its tooling-slice enum; ADOPT-001 §12.8 reference line omits D-048. One MIN: STATUS.md header date not updated. Eight of 10 carry-forward TFs correctly tracked as open for future slices; two implemented TFs (SET-EQ-001, TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001) not marked closed.\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-MAJ-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"STATUS.md TF entries for TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001 and TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ-001 remain marked '(open)' despite both being implemented in this slice and ratified by D-048.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"STATUS.md lines 346+352 show both TFs as '(open)'. DISPATCH-NOTE TF table states 'TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001 (this one IS closed by the slice's transform inclusion list)'. D-048 rationale: 'transform inclusion lists close the lock_branch / required_linear_history / block_creations posture gap (per R30 SAFE-MAJ-001)'. Set-equality verify IS at script:1095; ALLOWED_*_KEYS constants ARE at script:440-449.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Audit-trail inconsistency. Governance reviewers, future Codex dispatches, or 024C kickoff ceremony reading STATUS.md TF list would not know these TFs are closed, potentially re-opening resolved work or failing TF-count closure checks.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Update STATUS.md TF entries for TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001 and TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ-001 from '(open)' to '(closed: implemented in 024B-extras-2)'. Add closure date and reference to D-048 for each.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-MAJ-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Workflow guard inline simulation in test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh (run_workflow_guard_case, line ~207) has stale tooling-slice case statement missing '024B-extras-2'; STATUS.md claim of '2 test sites updated' is therefore inaccurate.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh line ~207: 'case \\\\\\\"$slice_id\\\\\\\" in\\\\\\\\n  024A|024B-core|024B-extras|024G)' — missing 024B-extras-2. Actual workflow file check-invocation-log-entry.yml line 68: '024A|024B-core|024B-extras|024B-extras-2|024G' — correctly includes it. STATUS.md step 2 (2026-05-13): 'Tooling-slice enum updated to include 024B-extras-2 at 2 test sites'. The inline simulation is a third site missed.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"If a workflow guard test case is added for 024B-extras-2, it will produce enforce=true instead of enforce=false, causing a test failure. More immediately, STATUS.md's coverage claim is inaccurate, masking the test gap from future fix-round reviewers.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Update the run_workflow_guard_case inline case statement at line ~207 to '024A|024B-core|024B-extras|024B-extras-2|024G'. Add a workflow guard test case verifying that a DISPATCH-NOTE with slice_id=024B-extras-2 produces enforce=false in GITHUB_OUTPUT. Correct STATUS.md step 2 to '3 test sites'.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-MAJ-003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"ADOPT-001 §12.8 reference line (line 1280) cites D-047, D-035, D-030 but omits D-048, leaving the automated Gate 3 governance record unreferenced from the procedure it governs.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"ADOPT-001 line 1280: 'Reference: D-047, WP-SCP-024 invariant 7, D-035, D-030, and the break-glass guidance in docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md.' D-048 is the ratifying decision for --expected-wrapper-sha automated Gate 3 and the permanence callout at ADOPT-001:1265. D-047's rationale explicitly says Gate 2 automated verification is absent from extras-1 and deferred to D-048.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"An operator consulting §12.8 to understand the trust-model basis for automated Gate 3 verification is not directed to D-048, the canonical governance record. Also inconsistent: the permanence callout (ADOPT-001:1265) is a D-048 contribution but D-047 is cited as the authority.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Update ADOPT-001 §12.8 reference line to: 'Reference: D-047 (core restore contract), D-048 (automated Gate 3 + permanence), WP-SCP-024 invariant 7, D-035, D-030, and the break-glass guidance in docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md.'\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-MIN-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"STATUS.md header 'Last updated: 2026-05-12' was not updated to 2026-05-13 when the 2026-05-13 chain entry was appended.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"STATUS.md line 2: '**Last updated:** 2026-05-12 (WP-SCP-024 024B-extras fix-round-31...)'. STATUS.md contains a '## Today's chain (2026-05-13 — 024B-extras-2 depth-defense surface)' section with 4 steps including D-048 filing.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Minor audit-trail confusion: the document's declared currency date is one day stale, causing the chain entry date and the header date to mismatch. Low risk but inconsistent with the standard STATUS.md maintenance procedure applied in all prior chains.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Update STATUS.md header to: '**Last updated:** 2026-05-13 (WP-SCP-024 024B-extras-2 depth-defense surface; D-048 filed)'.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"CG-nit-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"check-invocation-log-entry.yml was modified to add '024B-extras-2' to the tooling-slice short-circuit case (line 68), but this change was not listed in the DISPATCH-NOTE opening checklist.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Workflow file line 68: '024A|024B-core|024B-extras|024B-extras-2|024G'. DISPATCH-NOTE opening checklist (lines 120-129) does not mention the workflow file modification. The modification is correct and necessary (without it the CI would enforce invocation-log checks on this slice's own PR). But it is undocumented.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"Negligible operational impact since the modification is correct. Creates a minor discrepancy between the checklist and the actual scope — a governance-trace artifact for future slice authors referencing this slice as a pattern.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a note to the DISPATCH-NOTE opening checklist acknowledging the workflow tooling-slice enum update, or add a note to STATUS.md step 2 specifically calling out the workflow file as a 3rd site alongside the 2 already mentioned.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"d7682bb9-b6cb-4d92-8cd1-de011dab745e\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.14107335,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":11,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":148695,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":761667,\"output_tokens\":23477,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":148695,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":13009,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":133810,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":22393,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":22393},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":2634,\"outputTokens\":29,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.0027790000000000002,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":11,\"outputTokens\":23477,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":761667,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":148695,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.1382943500000002,\"contextWindow\":600000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"ec7614a6-f277-467b-b9d8-6de611240788\"}\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/r1-safety_bypass.json:1:{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":602966,\"duration_api_ms\":603679,\"num_turns\":16,\"result\":\"I now have all the information I need. Let me produce the findings report.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"lens\\\": \\\"safety_bypass\\\",\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"APPROVED_WITH_FINDINGS\\\",\\n  \\\"summary\\\": \\\"Four MAJ findings prevent fixpoint. (1) validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags() accepts any tag name matching the SHA — tag-name shape (vN.M.K) is never validated, so a non-release tag pushed to the SCP repo satisfies Gate 3 SHA validation. (2) GATE2_CAUTION_LINE is assembled with ${OPERATOR} at line 714, inside check_forward_mode_safety(), which runs before OPERATOR is set at line 1147 — the CAUTION log-block line records 'Operator @' with a blank username, breaking operator attribution in the load-bearing audit primitive. (3) D-048 explicitly claims --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification 'is only allowed when prior_restore_evidence_present returns true' — the code does not enforce this: when prior_restore_evidence_present() is false the flag is silently accepted, GATE2_CAUTION_LINE is never set, and no audit trace is produced. D-048 governance record is false. (4) TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-FILE-TOCTOU-001 is carried forward but not resolved: RESTORE_PRE_STATE is read twice from disk (cat line 870 vs validate_restore_source_json line 871); the canonical-context guard and all RESTORE_TARGET_* extractions use the raw cat read, not the validated payload — a file-swap between reads bypasses validation. Three MIN and one nit round out the surface. Set-equality verify phase, transform inclusion list, posture-degradation flag enumeration (all 7 present), and VERSIONING.md coverage (all 4 new flags listed) verified correct.\\\",\\n  \\\"findings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SB-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Tag name shape is not validated — any tag name matching the SHA satisfies Gate 3 SHA validation, not just vN.M.K release tags.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags() (lines 590–654): matched_tag is set to ${ref#refs/tags/} for the first ref whose SHA matches. No check that matched_tag matches /^v[0-9]+\\\\\\\\.[0-9]+\\\\\\\\.[0-9]+$/. Both lightweight (commit) and annotated (tag-object) paths set matched_tag unconditionally on SHA equality.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"An operator or CI job that can push any tag to jrnb2024/standards-control-plane (e.g., a ci-probe or test-deploy tag) pointing to a known commit SHA could satisfy --expected-wrapper-sha Gate 3 validation for that SHA even if no vN.M.K release tag exists. Tag-protection rulesets (D-030/D-034) provide partial mitigation but are not enforced in the code path.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"After resolving matched_tag, validate it against a regex: if ! printf '%s' \\\\\\\"$matched_tag\\\\\\\" | grep -qE '^v[0-9]+\\\\\\\\.[0-9]+\\\\\\\\.[0-9]+$'; then echo 'error: matched tag is not a vN.M.K release tag' >&2; exit 2; fi. Also add a test asserting that a non-vN.M.K tag name is rejected even when its SHA matches.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SB-002\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"GATE2_CAUTION_LINE is assigned with ${OPERATOR} expanding to empty string — the load-bearing audit-log CAUTION line records 'Operator @' with blank username.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"OPERATOR=\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\" (line 117 initial declaration). GATE2_CAUTION_LINE=\\\\\\\"...Operator @${OPERATOR} acknowledges...\\\\\\\" assigned inside check_forward_mode_safety() at line 714. OPERATOR is not set to the real username until line 1147 (gh api user). The heredoc at lines 1193–1230 expands ${GATE2_CAUTION_LINE} as an already-fixed string — re-expansion of ${OPERATOR} does not occur. Lines 1169/1205 (main 'Operator:' header) ARE correct because they expand ${OPERATOR} at heredoc-emit time.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"The CAUTION line — identified by D-048 and ADOPT-001 §12.8 as the auditable bypass record — omits operator identity. An auditor reviewing the log block cannot determine who invoked the bypass from the CAUTION line itself (though the header does carry the name). Breaks the forensic completeness of the audit primitive.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Move GATE2_CAUTION_LINE assignment to after OPERATOR is set at line 1147, or use a lazy-expansion pattern: use a placeholder and construct the final line at heredoc-emit time using a format string rather than a pre-assigned variable with early ${OPERATOR} substitution.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SB-003\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"D-048 falsely states --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification 'is only allowed when prior_restore_evidence_present returns true' — the code silently accepts the flag when prior_restore_evidence_present() is false, with no error and no audit trail.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"D-048 (line 102 of DECISIONS.md): 'the bypass is only allowed when prior_restore_evidence_present returns true'. Code: the if prior_restore_evidence_present block (line 707–721) is the only place ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION=1 has any effect. When the block is not entered (no prior evidence), the flag is accepted, GATE2_CAUTION_LINE stays \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\", no sleep fires, and no log-block caution is emitted. The top-level mutex checks (lines 298–306) block --expected-wrapper-sha combined with the flag but do not block the flag alone on cold-start.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"D-048 makes a false security assurance: auditors reading the governance record believe the flag is gated but it is not. A careless operator passing --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification on a fresh first-time enable gets no error and no audit trace; if prior_restore_evidence_present() is ever fooled (e.g., log-file tampering), the Gate 3 bypass produces zero audit signal.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add an explicit rejection early in check_forward_mode_safety(): if [ $ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION -eq 1 ] and prior_restore_evidence_present() is false, emit error 'prior restore evidence required for --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification' and exit 2. Then amend D-048 to accurately describe the enforcement. Add a test: cold-start repo + --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification → exit 2.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SB-004\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MAJ\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-FILE-TOCTOU-001 is unresolved: RESTORE_PRE_STATE is read twice from disk; a file-swap between reads can deliver a different payload to the canonical-context guard than what the validator accepted.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Line 870: RESTORE_TARGET_JSON=$(cat \\\\\\\"$RESTORE_PRE_STATE\\\\\\\"). Line 871: RESTORE_PAYLOAD=$(validate_restore_source_json \\\\\\\"$RESTORE_PRE_STATE\\\\\\\"). All RESTORE_TARGET_* variables (strict, contexts, admins, force-pushes, deletions) derive from RESTORE_TARGET_JSON (raw cat). The canonical-context guard at lines 946–963 uses RESTORE_TARGET_JSON. RESTORE_PAYLOAD (validated Python output) is used only for RESTORE_PUT_PAYLOAD and RESTORE_SIGNATURES_ENABLED. The carry-forward TF in DISPATCH-NOTE confirms this is a known open defect.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"A filesystem-level attacker (or a malicious operator) could serve a valid JSON to the Python validator on the second read while delivering a different JSON via the first cat read. The canonical-context guard and verify phase then operate against unvalidated content. Race window is narrow but the fix is trivial.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Read the file once into a variable: PRE_STATE_RAW=$(cat \\\\\\\"$RESTORE_PRE_STATE\\\\\\\"). Pass the content via stdin or env to validate_restore_source_json rather than the file path; have the function output the transformed payload from the same in-memory string. All subsequent uses of RESTORE_TARGET_JSON and RESTORE_PAYLOAD derive from the single read. Update validate_restore_source_json to accept stdin.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SB-005\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"--i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible is silently accepted (no error, no warning) when the wrapper IS readable, making the flag interface misleading with no posture downgrade.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Lines 740–762: the ACK_WRAPPER_INACCESSIBLE check appears only in the else branch (when wrapper_content is empty). When wrapper_content is non-empty, the if branch performs the verification and ACK_WRAPPER_INACCESSIBLE is never consulted. The top-level mutex only rejects it in --restore mode (lines 292–295). No guard rejects the flag in forward mode when wrapper is readable.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"An operator who passes the flag 'just in case' while the wrapper is readable sees no feedback. Verification still runs (no downgrade), but the operator cannot confirm which code path was taken. Under a social-engineering scenario, an attacker instructing an operator to 'add --i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible' might create false confidence that verification was bypassed.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"After wrapper verification succeeds (line 742 log), check if ACK_WRAPPER_INACCESSIBLE=1 and emit a warning: 'WARNING: --i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible passed but wrapper is readable; verification was performed normally. Remove the flag to suppress this warning.' This closes the silent-acceptance surface without changing security posture.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SB-006\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"RESTORE_PRE_STATE path is not realpath-resolved before file opens — symlink following is unrestricted at both the Python open() and the cat call.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"validate_restore_source_json opens sys.argv[1] via open(path) without os.path.realpath(). cat \\\\\\\"$RESTORE_PRE_STATE\\\\\\\" also follows symlinks. check-invocation-log-entry.sh uses resolve_inside_repo_root() / python3 os.path.realpath() for all its file paths (lines 130–143). No equivalent guard exists in enable-required-check.sh for RESTORE_PRE_STATE.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"A symlink at the RESTORE_PRE_STATE path that is swapped to point outside the repo root (or to a sensitive file) could be consumed without operator awareness. Combined with the TOCTOU issue in SB-004, a symlink swap during the read gap yields unvalidated content. Risk is low (requires local filesystem write access) but the defense is absent.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Resolve the path before use: RESTORE_PRE_STATE=$(python3 -c 'import os,sys; print(os.path.realpath(sys.argv[1]))' \\\\\\\"$RESTORE_PRE_STATE\\\\\\\"). Optionally assert the resolved path is under a known safe directory (e.g., the REPO_ROOT or CWD).\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SB-007\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"MIN\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"Wrapper grep uses line-by-line filtering that is not YAML-aware — multi-line YAML block scalars or anchor-alias patterns could diverge between grep-match and GitHub Actions runtime execution.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Line 741: grep -vE '^[[:space:]]*#' | grep -qE '^[[:space:]]*uses:[[:space:]]+[^#]*standards-control-plane[^#]*@SHA'. This strips comment lines and matches a uses: line. GitHub Actions YAML parser handles anchors, aliases, and folded/literal block scalars; grep does not. A crafted wrapper with a YAML anchor pointing the uses: value to a different string would pass grep (anchored line matches) while executing differently at runtime.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"In practice limited: GitHub Actions requires uses: to be a simple scalar string; block scalars and anchors are not supported for the uses: field. However, the grep approach cannot provide a formal guarantee of match-to-execution equivalence. Classification: defense correctness gap, not an active bypass path.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Add a note in ADOPT-001 §12.8 and the script's inline comment that the grep approach is heuristic; a future hardening step could fetch the raw YAML, parse it with python3's yaml.safe_load(), and extract .jobs.*.steps[].uses directly. For now, the practical risk is negligible given GitHub Actions' strict scalar constraint on uses:.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"SB-nit-001\\\",\\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"nit\\\",\\n      \\\"claim\\\": \\\"validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags() hardcodes 'repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/git/refs/tags' — the trailing hyphen and literal org/repo are brittle.\\\",\\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"Lines 593 and 638 use the literal string jrnb2024/standards-control-plane (note trailing hyphen). If this is the actual repo name it is fragile to rename; if it is a typo for standards-control-plane the function will always fail (no tags found → exit 2). The REPO_ROOT variable is available but not used to derive the remote URL.\\\",\\n      \\\"impact\\\": \\\"If the trailing hyphen is a typo, Gate 3 SHA validation always fails silently (exit 2 with 'SHA not found'), forcing operators to use --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification every time. Correctness hazard, not a security bypass.\\\",\\n      \\\"mitigation\\\": \\\"Derive the SCP repo identifier from git remote get-url origin or a top-level constant (SCP_REPO_SLUG). Verify the trailing hyphen is intentional or correct it. Add a test fixture that exercises the function against a known fake-tags response to catch URL regressions.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"e04f23e1-6099-42a7-854c-c0aabecb3e21\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.12453695,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":10,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":122335,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":522039,\"output_tokens\":33782,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":122335,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":\"\",\"iterations\":[{\"input_tokens\":1,\"output_tokens\":5889,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":125886,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":3957,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":3957},\"type\":\"message\"}],\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"modelUsage\":{\"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\":{\"inputTokens\":2264,\"outputTokens\":29,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":0,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":0,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":0.002409,\"contextWindow\":200000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000},\"claude-sonnet-4-6\":{\"inputTokens\":10,\"outputTokens\":33782,\"cacheReadInputTokens\":522039,\"cacheCreationInputTokens\":122335,\"webSearchRequests\":0,\"costUSD\":1.1221279499999999,\"contextWindow\":600000,\"maxOutputTokens\":32000}},\"permission_denials\":[],\"terminal_reason\":\"completed\",\"fast_mode_state\":\"off\",\"uuid\":\"6686d04c-9ffe-4fcd-b639-f81a5ea2d516\"}\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:1:# DISPATCH-NOTE — WP-SCP-024 slice 024B-extras-2 (depth-defense surface) — SKELETON\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:15:The depth-defense surface was extracted into this slice (024B-extras-2). The core --restore + ADOPT-001 §12.8 (manual Gate 3) + workflow CI gate shipped in 024B-extras-1 — that's what 024C cascade needs. This slice adds the automated Gate 3 verification + canonical-context guard + set-equality verify phase + transform inclusion-list defense + annotated-tag dereferencing.\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:34:| `--expected-wrapper-sha SHA` flag + `validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags()` | `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` | Re-add the function with annotated-tag dereferencing (gh api git/refs/tags/* via --paginate + per-annotated-tag git/tags/<sha> dereference). Validates supplied SHA against release-tag SHAs. |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:35:| `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` flag + conditional CAUTION/sleep | `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` | Re-add ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION + GATE2_CAUTION_LINE. CAUTION + 5s sleep fires ONLY when prior_restore_evidence_present (R16-CORR-002 closure). |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:36:| `--i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible` flag + wrapper-pin verification | `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` | Re-add ACK_WRAPPER_INACCESSIBLE + WRAPPER_INACCESSIBLE_CAUTION_LINE + gh api contents grep-anchored uses: match. |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:39:| Transform inclusion list | `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` | Add ALLOWED_REQUIRED_STATUS_CHECKS_KEYS / ALLOWED_REQUIRED_PR_REVIEWS_KEYS / ALLOWED_RESTRICTIONS_KEYS to transform(). |\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:56:### Option A — Rebase 024B-extras-2 onto merged 024B-extras-1\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:60:git rebase origin/main  # may have conflicts; resolve preferring 024B-extras-2's depth-defense additions\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:69:git diff <024B-extras-1-merge-SHA> feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-2 -- scripts/ tests/ docs/adoption/ docs/DECISIONS.md docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/ policies/ > /tmp/depth-defense.diff\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:71:# Stage + commit as one clean \"024B-extras-2 depth-defense surface\" commit\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:97:Target: 024B-extras-2 merged within ~4-5 hours wall-clock (smaller surface; R16's depth-finds already addressed).\ndocs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/DISPATCH-NOTE.md:114:| TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-FILE-TOCTOU-001 | extras-1 fix-round-21 | RESTORE_PRE_STATE TOCTOU hardening |\nSTATUS.md:40:- `required_status_checks: [\"policy-check / scp/policy-check\"]` (strict).\nSTATUS.md:164:| 1 | WP-SCP-024 024B-extras split via `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md` after 16 R-cycles; depth-defense surface carved to `024B-extras-2` (branch preserved at `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-2`). 024B-extras-1 = current branch with surface reduced to core `--restore` + ADOPT-001 §12.8 (manual Gate 3) + CI workflow + 6 of 6 posture-degradation flags. D-048 reserved. |\nSTATUS.md:181:| 9 | R28 surfaced **4th mock-masking-class defect**: fix-round-25's restructuring left required_signatures apply-decision broken on real-API multi-key `{url, enabled}` GET shape. `restore_signatures_enabled` now reuses Python-extracted RESTORE_SIGNATURES_ENABLED. Strict-must-be-boolean type check added for required_status_checks.strict. Closed in fix-round-29 (commit `0f1ba8e`). |\nSTATUS.md:184:## Today's chain (2026-05-13 — 024B-extras-2 depth-defense surface)\nSTATUS.md:188:| 1 | WP-SCP-024 024B-extras-2 depth-defense surface re-applied onto post-extras-1-merge main via targeted `git revert -n d2f5148` of the carve commit. Resolved 8 conflict regions in `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` (3 trivial flag-list unions kept BOTH extras-1 `--i-understand-restore-disables-strict-mode` AND depth-defense `--i-understand-restore-replaces-required-check-context`; 1 transform-inclusion-list took depth-defense side per TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001; 1 misaligned HEAD snippet discarded; 2 minor message refinements). ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 3 rewritten to use automated `--expected-wrapper-sha` verification + restored Post-break-glass permanence + audited `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` bypass. policies/VERSIONING.md branch-protection helper flag list extended with 4 depth-defense flags. |\nSTATUS.md:189:| 2 | Test surface restored from fd62641 (depth-defense lineage); single fix needed — `restore-null-status-checks` test updated to also pass `--i-understand-restore-disables-strict-mode` (the strict-mode acknowledgement was added in extras-1 R-rounds post-fd62641; previously-null required_status_checks normalises to {strict: false, contexts: []} so both flags are now required for that case). Tooling-slice enum `{024A, 024B-core, 024B-extras, 024G}` updated to include `024B-extras-2` at 2 test sites. |\nSTATUS.md:344:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-POLICY-CHECK-TARGET-FILTER-TESTS-001** (open): add per-test coverage for `lib/policy_check_invocation.sh` target-selection loop in 024B-extras-2 (or a future slice). The loop now has 2 path-based excludes (`tests/conflict_gate/fixtures/*` + the narrowed `docs/reviews/*/r1-*.json` + siblings); no direct tests exercise these. Surfaced by R23 fix-round-23 + R24 review of fix-round-24. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\nSTATUS.md:345:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-PUT-BODY-SHAPE-ASSERTIONS-001** (open): extend PUT-body shape assertions (`jq -e 'has($field) and .[$field] | type == \"boolean\"'` pattern) across ALL existing restore test cases in `tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh`. Fix-round-22 added shape assertions only for the new `restore-getshape-subresources` test; the older restore tests still trust the fake-gh PUT-body acceptance without strict-shape checks. Surfaced by step-7 demo + R22 + R25 against real GitHub API (the 3rd mock-masking CRIT in this slice's history). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\nSTATUS.md:346:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001** (open): `validate_restore_source_json()` `transform()` uses an exclusion-list approach — unknown GitHub branch-protection fields pass through to the PUT body. R30 surfaced `lock_branch`, `required_linear_history`, `block_creations` (and any future similar) pass through with NO posture-degradation guard, allowing a malicious pre-state to enable these without operator ack. Closure: switch to inclusion-list transform (explicitly allowed fields) + posture-degradation acknowledgement flags for each guarded sub-field. Aligns with the depth-defense surface carve (SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice (D-048); does NOT gate 024C — current exclusion list is sufficient for cohort onboarding under invariant 7's <30-min SLO since cohort pre-states are operator-captured from REAL adopter GET (not attacker-crafted).\nSTATUS.md:348:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-PATH-CONTAINMENT-001** (open): apply `resolve_inside_repo_root()` guard to `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <path>` argument in 024B-extras-2 alongside other defensive hardening. Low blast-radius (operator-credentials-bound). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\nSTATUS.md:349:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-COHORT-REGEX-MULTICHAR-001** (open): widen `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` cohort regex from `024[C-F]/` to `024[C-F][^/]*/` for future multi-char cohort slice IDs. Current 5-cohort set (024C/D/E/F) is single-char and unaffected; defensive. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\nSTATUS.md:351:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-STAGED-RESTORE-TEST-001** (open): add test case for staged-but-uncommitted prior-restore evidence in 024B-extras-2 tests (guards against future narrowing of `git diff HEAD` to `git diff`). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice.\nSTATUS.md:352:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ-001** (open): restore verify-phase set-equality comparison (deferred from 024B-extras-1 carve per `SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md`). Closure: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` verify phase uses jq sorted-set comparison for `required_status_checks.contexts`. NOT BLOCKING 024C — extras-1's substring grep -F is sufficient for cohort onboarding under invariant 7's <30-min SLO. Owns: 024B-extras-2 slice. Does NOT gate 024C.\nSTATUS.md:353:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-FILE-TOCTOU-001** (open): `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` reads RESTORE_PRE_STATE file three separate times (cat to RESTORE_TARGET_JSON, validate_restore_source_json, inline Python signatures extract). Mitigation: read once into a variable and pipe content to validate + signature-extract via stdin. Defensive hardening; current posture-degradation flag gates bound the blast radius. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\nSTATUS.md:354:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-WORKFLOW-PIN-BASE-BRANCH-001** (open): `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` invokes `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` from the PR's checked-out code (PR HEAD), not the base branch. For future multi-operator adoption, pin enforcement to `git show origin/main:scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh | bash -s -- ...` or use a reusable workflow from base. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice (depth-defense); does NOT gate 024C.\nSTATUS.md:355:- **TF-024B-REQCHECK-ENABLE-001** (open): Before 024C dispatch opens, operator must add `check-invocation-log-entry / check-invocation-log-entry` to main branch's `required_status_checks` list via `gh api -X PATCH repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/branches/main/protection` with the updated contexts list, then record the SCP-self REQCHECK enablement as a `STATUS.md` chain entry only. Do NOT modify `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md`; that log is reserved for adopter-side `enable-required-check.sh` invocations per D-035 scope. Without this step CI-enforcement is advisory only (the workflow runs but doesn't block merge). Close as part of 024C kickoff ceremony.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:876:   gh api repos/OWNER/NAME/branches/BRANCH/protection/required_status_checks \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:938:   gh api repos/OWNER/NAME/branches/BRANCH/protection/required_status_checks --jq '.contexts'\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:945:   gh api -X PATCH repos/OWNER/NAME/branches/BRANCH/protection/required_status_checks \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:951:   gh api -X PATCH repos/OWNER/NAME/branches/BRANCH/protection/required_status_checks \\\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1217:  non-empty `required_status_checks.contexts` that does NOT contain the\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1265:> **Post-break-glass permanence:** After any break-glass cycle, all subsequent forward-mode `enable-required-check.sh` invocations for the same adopter permanently require `--expected-wrapper-sha` (or `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` with CAUTION audit). This is intentional: once an adopter has hit a break-glass, we demand operator-explicit SHA confirmation on every re-enable for the rest of the adopter's lifetime. The restore log entry in git history is the authoritative record; force-push to main is disabled (D-030) so the entry cannot be expunged.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1276:> **CAUTION.** When the bypass flag is used, the helper emits a caution line in the invocation log block, prints a CAUTION line to standard error, and pauses 5 seconds before any API mutation so the operator can abort with Ctrl-C if the flag was passed unintentionally. Use it only when the operator is intentionally prioritising recovery over wrapper-pin verification.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1278:> **🛑 CAUTION:** Re-enabling required-check while the adopter wrapper is pinned to a broken/unfixed SHA will block ALL future PR merges on the adopter repo until manually unpinned. There is no scriptable rollback for this misuse - the operator must run `--restore` again with the pre-Gate-1 captured pre-state JSON.\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:8:#   - required_status_checks.contexts = [\"${SCP_REQUIRED_CONTEXT}\"]\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:11:#   - required_status_checks.strict = true (PR must be up-to-date\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:117:OPERATOR=\"\"\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:123:RESTORE_PRE_STATE=\"\"\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:133:ACK_NO_GATE2_VERIFICATION=0\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh:135:GATE2_CAUTION_LINE=\"\"\ns