cs/DECISIONS.md:101:| D-047 | 2026-05-10 | Adopt WP-SCP-024 024B-extras operational contracts: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <pre-state.json>` restores branch protection from the captured prior-state log entry by transforming GET-shape JSON into the PUT body, stripping envelope fields recursively, converting `enforce_admins.enabled` to a boolean, and replaying `required_signatures` through the dedicated sub-resource; restore-mode posture-degradation flags `--i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement`, `--i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks`, `--i-understand-restore-disables-strict-mode`, `--i-understand-restore-disables-required-signatures`, `--i-understand-restore-re-enables-force-pushes`, and `--i-understand-restore-re-enables-deletions` are mandatory when the target removes or re-enables those protections; forward-mode now performs a path-pinned workflow lookup for `.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml` and queries workflow-runs without a branch filter; the new CI workflow `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` wires the CLI gate into PR checks with `paths: docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[C-Z]*/**` plus explicit branch-protection-log.md / STATUS.md triggers and tooling-slice short-circuiting; ADOPT-001 gains §12.8 break-glass procedure with manual Gate 3 verification; STATUS.md and the DISPATCH-NOTE placeholder for the step-7 operator demo are updated in-slice. The depth-defense surface (wrapper-SHA verification, canonical-context guard, set-equality verify) is carved into sibling slice 024B-extras-2 per `SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md`; D-048 reserved for that slice. | ACCEPTED | The 024B split left the restore / break-glass / workflow-integration surface as the deferred half so the review load stayed bounded. This decision ratifies the operational contract that lets operators disable and re-enable the federation primitive safely without widening the adopter-facing API surface, while preserving the bootstrap guard that prevents tooling slices from self-blocking their own PRs. The release-tag SHA requirement is intentionally anchored to actual git tags, not arbitrary commits, so Gate 3 can re-arm against a concrete release artifact rather than against moving main-head. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: the helper remains operator-run, the escape hatch is explicitly auditable, and the restore demo evidence is still an operator-interactive step outside Codex dispatch. Gate 2 automated wrapper-SHA verification is absent in extras-1; the trust-model gap is deferred to D-048 / 024B-extras-2, which will add an `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` flag for explicit operator acknowledgement when Gate 2 verification is skipped. Identified at WP-SCP-024 024B-extras authoring time. |\ndocs/DECISIONS.md:102:| D-048 | 2026-05-13 | Adopt the WP-SCP-024 024B-extras-2 depth-defense surface as estate doctrine. Components: (1) `--expected-wrapper-sha SHA` flag + `validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags()` validates the supplied SHA against `gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/git/refs/tags?per_page=100` with annotated-tag dereferencing (per-annotated-tag `gh api git/tags/<sha>` follow-up to resolve to commit SHA), so Gate 3 SHA-pinning works regardless of whether SCP-self uses lightweight or annotated release tags. (2) `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` flag is the audited Gate 2 bypass: emits a CAUTION line to stderr, a `GATE2_CAUTION_LINE` row in the invocation-log block, and pauses 5 seconds before any API mutation so operators can Ctrl-C if the flag was passed unintentionally; the bypass is only allowed when `prior_restore_evidence_present` returns true (Gate 3 re-enable post-break-glass), so cold-start adopters cannot accidentally bypass Gate 2. (3) `--i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible` flag is required when the adopter wrapper file (`.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml`) cannot be read from the current context — without the flag, the script refuses to continue rather than silently degrading to a CAUTION-only audit note. (4) `--i-understand-restore-replaces-required-check-context` flag is the canonical-context guard: when the restore target has a non-empty `required_status_checks.contexts` set that does NOT contain the canonical SCP check (`REQUIRED_CONTEXT`, default `policy-check / scp/policy-check`), restore mode requires this flag, preventing an attacker-modified pre-state JSON from silently replacing the policy gate with attacker-controlled context. (5) Set-equality verify phase replaces the prior comma-substring `grep -F` comparison with a jq `--argjson expected_contexts ... sort == sort` element-wise comparison, so legitimate restores no longer fail spuriously when GitHub returns contexts in a different order than the pre-state JSON. (6) Transform inclusion lists (`ALLOWED_REQUIRED_STATUS_CHECKS_KEYS`, `ALLOWED_REQUIRED_PULL_REQUEST_REVIEW_KEYS`, `ALLOWED_RESTRICTIONS_KEYS`) replace the prior exclusion-list shape in `transform()` — only documented fields pass through to the PUT body; unknown nested fields are dropped rather than leaked. (7) Mutex checks reject incompatible flag combinations (`--restore + --expected-wrapper-sha`, `--restore + --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification`, `--restore + --i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible`, `--expected-wrapper-sha + --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification`, `--expected-wrapper-sha + --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci`). ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 3 is rewritten to use `--expected-wrapper-sha` automated wrapper-pin verification (replacing the manual procedure from extras-1); the Post-break-glass permanence callout is restored. `policies/VERSIONING.md` lists all 4 new posture-degradation flags as breaking-change-protected. | ACCEPTED | The depth-defense surface was operator-decided to carve out of 024B-extras after 16 R-cycles + 38 hours of session wall-time plateaued at ~5 MAJ per round, with most findings being latent depth-defects in the depth-defense surface itself (per `SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md` + `feedback_asymptotic_trajectory_split.md`). The core `--restore` + manual-Gate-3 + workflow CI shipped in 024B-extras-1 (D-047); this slice (024B-extras-2) ratifies the depth-defense additions as separable safety properties, each adding a real defensive value: automated Gate 3 SHA-pinning eliminates operator-error on wrapper-pin verification; canonical-context guard prevents pre-state-tampering attacks; set-equality verify removes a brittle string-substring comparison; transform inclusion lists close the lock_branch / required_linear_history / block_creations posture gap (per R30 SAFE-MAJ-001); annotated-tag dereferencing makes Gate 3 work regardless of tag-format choice. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: the helper remains operator-run, the bypass flags are explicitly auditable via stderr CAUTION + log-block CAUTION entries; the 2026-07-21 quarterly review re-evaluates single-operator posture for break-glass procedures. Identified at WP-SCP-024 024B-extras carve point (SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md) + D-048 reservation. |\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:205:      slice_id=\"$(basename \"$(dirname \"$dispatch_note\")\")\"\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:206:      case \"$slice_id\" in\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:212:          echo \"Tooling slice ($slice_id); no enforcement needed.\"\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:851:  \"required_status_checks\": {\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:877:  \"required_status_checks\": {\"strict\": true, \"contexts\": [\"policy-check / scp/policy-check\"]},\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:886:  \"required_status_checks\": {\"strict\": true, \"contexts\": [\"policy-check / scp/policy-check\"]},\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:918:  \"required_status_checks\": {\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check