 7 operator-interactive demo). Split is incremental delivery, NOT descope - both halves still ship; both required before 024C cohort onboarding opens. Original 024B work preserved at `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-parking` branch (audit trail: 7 codex-fix-round-N-audit.log files + 7 R-round archive directories incl r8-archive carry-forward findings). Slice 024B-core scope is internally coherent: scaffolder generates adopter artefacts; CI enforcement script (CLI) validates cascade-status declarations; tests cover both. The CLI script can be invoked manually as a stop-gap until 024B-extras wires it into GitHub Actions. The CLI guard is necessary-but-not-sufficient: workflow-side hardcoding of `--tooling-slice-id` and omission of `--allow-not-applicable` in 024B-extras is the canonical closure path for the operator-supplied not-applicable bypass surface (see FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001). Bus-factor-1 acknowledged (D-031); 2026-07-21 quarterly review covers. Identified at WP-SCP-024 plan-doc §9 D-044 reservation |\n| D-047 | 2026-05-10 | Adopt WP-SCP-024 024B-extras operational contracts: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <pre-state.json>` restores branch protection from the captured prior-state log entry by transforming GET-shape JSON into the PUT body, stripping envelope fields recursively, converting `enforce_admins.enabled` to a boolean, and replaying `required_signatures` through the dedicated sub-resource; restore-mode posture-degradation flags `--i-understand-restore-removes-admin-enforcement`, `--i-understand-restore-removes-required-checks`, `--i-understand-restore-disables-strict-mode`, `--i-understand-restore-disables-required-signatures`, `--i-understand-restore-re-enables-force-pushes`, and `--i-understand-restore-re-enables-deletions` are mandatory when the target removes or re-enables those protections; forward-mode now performs a path-pinned workflow lookup for `.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml` and queries workflow-runs without a branch filter; the new CI workflow `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` wires the CLI gate into PR checks with `paths: docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024[C-Z]*/**` plus explicit branch-protection-log.md / STATUS.md triggers and tooling-slice short-circuiting; ADOPT-001 gains §12.8 break-glass procedure with manual Gate 3 verification; STATUS.md and the DISPATCH-NOTE placeholder for the step-7 operator demo are updated in-slice. The depth-defense surface (wrapper-SHA verification, canonical-context guard, set-equality verify) is carved into sibling slice 024B-extras-2 per `SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md`; D-048 reserved for that slice. | ACCEPTED | The 024B split left the restore / break-glass / workflow-integration surface as the deferred half so the review load stayed bounded. This decision ratifies the operational contract that lets operators disable and re-enable the federation primitive safely without widening the adopter-facing API surface, while preserving the bootstrap guard that prevents tooling slices from self-blocking their own PRs. The release-tag SHA requirement is intentionally anchored to actual git tags, not arbitrary commits, so Gate 3 can re-arm against a concrete release artifact rather than against moving main-head. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: the helper remains operator-run, the escape hatch is explicitly auditable, and the restore demo evidence is still an operator-interactive step outside Codex dispatch. Gate 2 automated wrapper-SHA verification is absent in extras-1; the trust-model gap is deferred to D-048 / 024B-extras-2, which will add an `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` flag for explicit operator acknowledgement when Gate 2 verification is skipped. Identified at WP-SCP-024 024B-extras authoring time. |\n| D-048 | 2026-05-13 | Adopt the WP-SCP-024 024B-extras-2 depth-defense surface as estate doctrine. Components: (1) `--expected-wrapper-sha SHA` flag + `validate_expected_wrapper_sha_against_tags()` validates the supplied SHA against `gh api repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/git/refs/tags?per_page=100` with annotated-tag dereferencing (per-annotated-tag `gh api git/tags/<sha>` follow-up to resolve to commit SHA), so Gate 3 SHA-pinning works regardless of whether SCP-self uses lightweight or annotated release tags. (2) `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` flag is the audited Gate 2 bypass: emits a CAUTION line to stderr, a `GATE2_CAUTION_LINE` row in the invocation-log block, and pauses 5 seconds before any API mutation so operators can Ctrl-C if the flag was passed unintentionally; the bypass is only allowed when `prior_restore_evidence_present` returns true (Gate 3 re-enable post-break-glass), so cold-start adopters cannot accidentally bypass Gate 2. (3) `--i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible` flag is required when the adopter wrapper file (`.github/workflows/policy-check-wrapper.yml`) cannot be read from the current context — without the flag, the script refuses to continue rather than silently degrading to a CAUTION-only audit note. (4) `--i-understand-restore-replaces-required-check-context` flag is the canonical-context guard: when the restore target has a non-empty `required_status_checks.contexts` set that does NOT contain the canonical SCP check (`REQUIRED_CONTEXT`, default `policy-check / scp/policy-check`), restore mode requires this flag, preventing an attacker-modified pre-state JSON from silently replacing the policy gate with attacker-controlled context. (5) Set-equality verify phase replaces the prior comma-substring `grep -F` comparison with a jq `--argjson expected_contexts ... sort == sort` element-wise comparison, so legitimate restores no longer fail spuriously when GitHub returns contexts in a different order than the pre-state JSON. (6) Transform inclusion lists (`ALLOWED_REQUIRED_STATUS_CHECKS_KEYS`, `ALLOWED_REQUIRED_PULL_REQUEST_REVIEW_KEYS`, `ALLOWED_RESTRICTIONS_KEYS`) replace the prior exclusion-list shape in `transform()` — only documented fields pass through to the PUT body; unknown nested fields are dropped rather than leaked. (7) Mutex checks reject incompatible flag combinations (`--restore + --expected-wrapper-sha`, `--restore + --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification`, `--restore + --i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible`, `--expected-wrapper-sha + --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification`, `--expected-wrapper-sha + --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci`). ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 3 is rewritten to use `--expected-wrapper-sha` automated wrapper-pin verification (replacing the manual procedure from extras-1); the Post-break-glass permanence callout is restored. `policies/VERSIONING.md` lists all 4 new posture-degradation flags as breaking-change-protected. | ACCEPTED | The depth-defense surface was operator-decided to carve out of 024B-extras after 16 R-cycles + 38 hours of session wall-time plateaued at ~5 MAJ per round, with most findings being latent depth-defects in the depth-defense surface itself (per `SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md` + `feedback_asymptotic_trajectory_split.md`). The core `--restore` + manual-Gate-3 + workflow CI shipped in 024B-extras-1 (D-047); this slice (024B-extras-2) ratifies the depth-defense additions as separable safety properties, each adding a real defensive value: automated Gate 3 SHA-pinning eliminates operator-error on wrapper-pin verification; canonical-context guard prevents pre-state-tampering attacks; set-equality verify removes a brittle string-substring comparison; transform inclusion lists close the lock_branch / required_linear_history / block_creations posture gap (per R30 SAFE-MAJ-001); annotated-tag dereferencing makes Gate 3 work regardless of tag-format choice. Bus-factor-1 acknowledged: the helper remains operator-run, the bypass flags are explicitly auditable via stderr CAUTION + log-block CAUTION entries; the 2026-07-21 quarterly review re-evaluates single-operator posture for break-glass procedures. Identified at WP-SCP-024 024B-extras carve point (SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md) + D-048 reservation. |\n\n> D-044 limitation note: the CLI guard is necessary-but-not-sufficient. 024B-extras must hardcode `--tooling-slice-id` per workflow file and omit `--allow-not-applicable` from cohort workflows; that workflow-side hardcoding is the canonical closure path for the operator-supplied not-applicable bypass surface (see FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001).\n\n=====\n- ~~**020H.2**: Regal binary SHA256 verification — closes TF-020H3-001~~ ✅ landed 2026-05-01 (PR #77, commit `bac1427`); 3-round recursive review reaching fixpoint at R2 (0 CRIT + 0 MAJ), 3 MAJ + 5 MIN + 13 nit closed; closed 13 days ahead of the 2026-05-14 deadline.\n- ~~**020H.3**: release-gate workflow (closes TF-005 + TF-020H1-001)~~ ✅ landed 2026-05-01 (PR #79, commit `42f49db`); 2-round recursive review reaching fixpoint at R2 (0 CRIT + 0 MAJ on all 3 lenses), 1 CRIT + 7 MAJ + 10 MIN + 10 nit closed across 2 fix-rounds. Architectural framing: workflow is observer/annotator (post-tag), not pre-emptive gate; pre-emptive enforcement is the operator's mandatory dry-run pre-flight discipline. Opened TF-020H3rg-001..003.\n- ~~**020H.3.1**: release-gate auto-issue (closes TF-020H3rg-003)~~ ✅ landed 2026-05-01 (PR #80, commit `d3e3c73`); 2-round recursive review reaching fixpoint at R2 with R2 safety clean APPROVED (0 findings), 1 MAJ + 8 MIN + 6 nit + 1 fix-round-1 self-correction closed. Two-job split: release-gate (contents:read) + release-gate-violation-issue (issues:write at job level per D-037). Filed TF-020H3rg-004.\n- ~~**020H.4**: rule-config disable canary (closes TF-020H1-004)~~ ✅ landed 2026-05-01 (PR #82, commit `c67a91a`); 2-round recursive review reaching fixpoint at R2 (0 CRIT + 0 MAJ on all 3 lenses), 1 MAJ + 6 MIN + 8 nit closed. New `canary/rule-config-disabled` branch (PR #81 DO-NOT-MERGE; SHA `841d350`) verified PASS at workflow run `25211284467`; `scripts/replay-canary.sh` registry extended; `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/canary-evidence.md` Canary 4 baseline section added. Suppression-path coverage triad complete (deny / waiver / rule-config). Opened TF-020H4-001..003.\n- ~~**SCP-073.sec**: `SECURITY.md` publication (security disclosure path for policy-bypass reports)~~ ✅ landed 2026-05-01 in 020H.1 fix-round-1 (commit `3817384`); `SECURITY.md` at repo root with GitHub Security Advisory + `jimbrooke@me.com` channels, 3-business-day SLA, 30-day coordinated-disclosure target; ADOPT-001 §12.7.8 + `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/rule-regression.md` updated to reference it directly. Closes WP-SCP-020 §4.1 SCP-073.sec forward-looking flag.\n- ~~**TF-020H3rg-002**: pip install --require-hashes for both YAML/JSON-validating workflows~~ ✅ landed 2026-05-02 in slice 020M (PR #84, commit `0e24cc6`); cut v1.0.1 PATCH.\n- ~~**WP-SCP-022 proposal-queue**: structured proposal queue for new rules.~~ ✅ Phase 1 closed 2026-05-02 in slice **020L** (PR #89, commit `25db685`) — RFC-001 / SCP-R-004 (waiver `reason` must cite issue/PR URL) authored, R1+R2 fixpoint, merged via operator-discretion early-merge per D-040. ✅ **Phase 2** closed 2026-05-02 in slice **020P** (PR #91, commit `d83ce52`) — `policies/SCP-R-004.rego` + 21 Conftest tests + conflict-gate fixtures + workflow warn-baseline rendering + ADOPT-001 §12.7.14 + RULE-TEMPLATE.md §5 + README.md §3 amendments + **v1.1.0 tag cut** (`https://github.com/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/releases/tag/v1.1.0`). Closes TF-020L-002 + TF-020L-003. Filed TF-020P-001/002/003/004/005.\n- **WP-SCP-023**: cross-repo scorecards.\n- **WP-SCP-024**: estate cascade (FLA pilot → PIM/recommender/etc.).\n\n## Tracked-forward items from WP-SCP-024 024B-core / 024B-extras\n\n- **FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001** (open): per-repo dispatcher install pattern resolved in ACC. install_acc_hook.sh currently hardcodes ROOT_DIR via BASH_SOURCE so each adopter repo would need its own install ceremony. 024C MUST NOT open until closed. ACC-side work item; SCP-side awaits closure. Owner: @jrnb2024.\n- **FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001** (closed in fix-round-4; this commit): 024B-extras workflow wiring now skips script invocation entirely for tooling slices, so the residual operator-supplied `not applicable` bypass surface is gone without passing `--allow-not-applicable` or `--tooling-slice-id` into the script. Cohort cascade slices still invoke the script with full enforcement; defense-in-depth now comes from the workflow short-circuit plus the script's default refusal of `--allow-not-applicable`.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-POLICY-CHECK-TARGET-FILTER-TESTS-001** (open): add per-test coverage for `lib/policy_check_invocation.sh` target-selection loop in 024B-extras-2 (or a future slice). The loop now has 2 path-based excludes (`tests/conflict_gate/fixtures/*` + the narrowed `docs/reviews/*/r1-*.json` + siblings); no direct tests exercise these. Surfaced by R23 fix-round-23 + R24 review of fix-round-24. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-PUT-BODY-SHAPE-ASSERTIONS-001** (open): extend PUT-body shape assertions (`jq -e 'has($field) and .[$field] | type == \"boolean\"'` pattern) across ALL existing restore test cases in `tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh`. Fix-round-22 added shape assertions only for the new `restore-getshape-subresources` test; the older restore tests still trust the fake-gh PUT-body acceptance without strict-shape checks. Surfaced by step-7 demo + R22 + R25 against real GitHub API (the 3rd mock-masking CRIT in this slice's history). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001** (open): `validate_restore_source_json()` `transform()` uses an exclusion-list approach — unknown GitHub branch-protection fields pass through to the PUT body. R30 surfaced `lock_branch`, `required_linear_history`, `block_creations` (and any future similar) pass through with NO posture-degradation guard, allowing a malicious pre-state to enable these without operator ack. Closure: switch to inclusion-list transform (explicitly allowed fields) + posture-degradation acknowledgement flags for each guarded sub-field. Aligns with the depth-defense surface carve (SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice (D-048); does NOT gate 024C — current exclusion list is sufficient for cohort onboarding under invariant 7's <30-min SLO since cohort pre-states are operator-captured from REAL adopter GET (not attacker-crafted).\n- **TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001** (closed 2026-05-11): --restore real-repo round-trip evidence at `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence.md` — operator-interactive demo at dispatch-plan step 7 completed against `jrnb2024/scp-024b-extras-restore-test` throw-away repo. **Surfaced CRIT** (mock-masking: transform did not unwrap `*.enabled` sub-objects for `required_linear_history`/`allow_force_pushes`/etc → HTTP 422 on real PUT); closed in fix-round-22 with generic `{enabled: bool}` unwrap + PUT-body-shape assertion test. Round-trip succeeded post-fix; all 4 key fields matched state-A target. Throw-away repo cleanup deferred — current gh token lacks `delete_repo` scope.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-PATH-CONTAINMENT-001** (open): apply `resolve_inside_repo_root()` guard to `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <path>` argument in 024B-extras-2 alongside other defensive hardening. Low blast-radius (operator-credentials-bound). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-COHORT-REGEX-MULTICHAR-001** (open): widen `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` cohort regex from `024[C-F]/` to `024[C-F][^/]*/` for future multi-char cohort slice IDs. Current 5-cohort set (024C/D/E/F) is single-char and unaffected; defensive. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-STEP7-FIXTURE-SEQ-001** (open): align DISPATCH-NOTE step-7 fixture sequence with `restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md` (add or harmonise `Mutate branch protection` step description). Will be resolved naturally at step-7 demo execution time.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-STAGED-RESTORE-TEST-001** (open): add test case for staged-but-uncommitted prior-restore evidence in 024B-extras-2 tests (guards against future narrowing of `git diff HEAD` to `git diff`). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ-001** (open): restore verify-phase set-equality comparison (deferred from 024B-extras-1 carve per `SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md`). Closure: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` verify phase uses jq sorted-set comparison for `required_status_checks.contexts`. NOT BLOCKING 024C — extras-1's substring grep -F is sufficient for cohort onboarding under invariant 7's <30-min SLO. Owns: 024B-extras-2 slice. Does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-FILE-TOCTOU-001** (open): `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` reads RESTORE_PRE_STATE file three separate times (cat to RESTORE_TARGET_JSON, validate_restore_source_json, inline Python signatures extract). Mitigation: read once into a variable and pipe content to validate + signature-extract via stdin. Defensive hardening; current posture-degradation flag gates bound the blast radius. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-WORKFLOW-PIN-BASE-BRANCH-001** (open): `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` invokes `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` from the PR's checked-out code (PR HEAD), not the base branch. For future multi-operator adoption, pin enforcement to `git show origin/main:scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh | bash -s -- ...` or use a reusable workflow from base. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice (depth-defense); does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-REQCHECK-ENABLE-001** (open): Before 024C dispatch opens, operator must add `check-invocation-log-entry / check-invocation-log-entry` to main branch's `required_status_checks` list via `gh api -X PATCH repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/branches/main/protection` with the updated contexts list, then record the SCP-self REQCHECK enablement as a `STATUS.md` chain entry only. Do NOT modify `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md`; that log is reserved for adopter-side `enable-required-check.sh` invocations per D-035 scope. Without this step CI-enforcement is advisory only (the workflow runs but doesn't block merge). Close as part of 024C kickoff ceremony.\n- **TF-024B-SCAFFOLDER-023E002-UPDATE** (open): when TF-023E-002 closes, remove the post-v1.2.0 warning block from `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` and delete the cutover ancestry guard that keeps the v1.0.0 fallback recommendation alive. The scaffolder should stop warning only after the separate `attest-scorecard` workflow restructuring lands. Owner: @jrnb2024.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
