M → control-tower → mapp-doc-agent + recommender → shopify-app; per-adopter onboarding contract (adopter PR + SCP-side cascade slice + invocation log + post-bake observation window ≥1 calendar week + ≥1 Renovate bump cycle). Reserves D-044/D-045/D-046 for implementation slices 024B/024C/024G. Threshold A: ≥3 of 5 cohort adopters required-check live + ≥1 SCP minor version-bump propagated cleanly via Renovate + USER-GATE-E signed. Required-check cascade is primary deliverable; scorecard-emit opt-in is secondary follow-up gated on TF-023E-002 closure, and 024B-core now warns on post-v1.2.0 SHAs while keeping the v1.0.0 pin as the operational fallback until TF-023E-002 closes. **Cascade-status spec hardened over 9 review rounds** (32 unique MAJ + 1 CRIT closed across 8 fix-rounds — unprecedented; cause was the cascade-status / CI-enforcement clause being structurally cross-cutting): 3 close-states (`onboarded`, `onboarded-operator-bump`, `blocked-on-adopter-conflict`) × 4 CI behaviours (3 named + fail-closed default) × (positive evidence + machine-enforceable regex format spec + negative assertion). WP-SCP-024 is the natural successor to the 5-move MVCP — turns SCP's estate observability (WP-SCP-023) into action. Merged at `4dc3faa`. |\nSTATUS.md:164:| 1 | WP-SCP-024 024B-extras split via `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md` after 16 R-cycles; depth-defense surface carved to `024B-extras-2` (branch preserved at `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-2`). 024B-extras-1 = current branch with surface reduced to core `--restore` + ADOPT-001 §12.8 (manual Gate 3) + CI workflow + 6 of 6 posture-degradation flags. D-048 reserved. |\nSTATUS.md:178:| 6 | R25 returned 7 raw MAJ → 3 REAL doc-only MAJ + 1 MIN after dedup + carve-filter (others DEFERRED to TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ-001 / extras-2 carve). Closed in fix-round-26 (commit `7ae3786`): evidence file SHA fill, plan-doc tooling enum, STATUS chain annotation, CLI tooling enum. |\nSTATUS.md:182:| 10 | R29 surfaced 1 MAJ awk false-positive on prior-restore-evidence detection (context lines from existing entries triggered exit 2); closed in fix-round-30 (commit `bde5db2`) with added-line guard in awk. R30 surfaced 2 REAL MAJ: CORR-002 covered by existing TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-PUT-BODY-SHAPE-ASSERTIONS-001; SAFE-MAJ-001 (transform exclusion-list gap allowing lock_branch/required_linear_history/block_creations through unchecked) filed as TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001. Slice at criterion (b): 0 CRIT + REAL MAJ all DEFERRED to extras-2 TFs. Merge per D-040 with documented protocol-deviation rationale. |\nSTATUS.md:184:## Today's chain (2026-05-13 — 024B-extras-2 depth-defense surface)\nSTATUS.md:188:| 1 | WP-SCP-024 024B-extras-2 depth-defense surface re-applied onto post-extras-1-merge main via targeted `git revert -n d2f5148` of the carve commit. Resolved 8 conflict regions in `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` (3 trivial flag-list unions kept BOTH extras-1 `--i-understand-restore-disables-strict-mode` AND depth-defense `--i-understand-restore-replaces-required-check-context`; 1 transform-inclusion-list took depth-defense side per TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001; 1 misaligned HEAD snippet discarded; 2 minor message refinements). ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 3 rewritten to use automated `--expected-wrapper-sha` verification + restored Post-break-glass permanence + audited `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` bypass. policies/VERSIONING.md branch-protection helper flag list extended with 4 depth-defense flags. |\nSTATUS.md:189:| 2 | Test surface restored from fd62641 (depth-defense lineage); single fix needed — `restore-null-status-checks` test updated to also pass `--i-understand-restore-disables-strict-mode` (the strict-mode acknowledgement was added in extras-1 R-rounds post-fd62641; previously-null required_status_checks normalises to {strict: false, contexts: []} so both flags are now required for that case). Tooling-slice enum `{024A, 024B-core, 024B-extras, 024G}` updated to include `024B-extras-2` at 2 test sites. |\nSTATUS.md:344:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-POLICY-CHECK-TARGET-FILTER-TESTS-001** (open): add per-test coverage for `lib/policy_check_invocation.sh` target-selection loop in 024B-extras-2 (or a future slice). The loop now has 2 path-based excludes (`tests/conflict_gate/fixtures/*` + the narrowed `docs/reviews/*/r1-*.json` + siblings); no direct tests exercise these. Surfaced by R23 fix-round-23 + R24 review of fix-round-24. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\nSTATUS.md:345:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-PUT-BODY-SHAPE-ASSERTIONS-001** (open): extend PUT-body shape assertions (`jq -e 'has($field) and .[$field] | type == \"boolean\"'` pattern) across ALL existing restore test cases in `tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh`. Fix-round-22 added shape assertions only for the new `restore-getshape-subresources` test; the older restore tests still trust the fake-gh PUT-body acceptance without strict-shape checks. Surfaced by step-7 demo + R22 + R25 against real GitHub API (the 3rd mock-masking CRIT in this slice's history). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\nSTATUS.md:346:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): `validate_restore_source_json()` `transform()` uses an exclusion-list approach — unknown GitHub branch-protection fields pass through to the PUT body. R30 surfaced `lock_branch`, `required_linear_history`, `block_creations` (and any future similar) pass through with NO posture-degradation guard, allowing a malicious pre-state to enable these without operator ack. Closure: switch to inclusion-list transform (explicitly allowed fields) + posture-degradation acknowledgement flags for each guarded sub-field. Aligns with the depth-defense surface carve (SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice (D-048); does NOT gate 024C — current exclusion list is sufficient for cohort onboarding under invariant 7's <30-min SLO since cohort pre-states are operator-captured from REAL adopter GET (not attacker-crafted).\nSTATUS.md:348:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-PATH-CONTAINMENT-001** (open): apply `resolve_inside_repo_root()` guard to `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <path>` argument in 024B-extras-2 alongside other defensive hardening. Low blast-radius (operator-credentials-bound). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\nSTATUS.md:349:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-COHORT-REGEX-MULTICHAR-001** (open): widen `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` cohort regex from `024[C-F]/` to `024[C-F][^/]*/` for future multi-char cohort slice IDs. Current 5-cohort set (024C/D/E/F) is single-char and unaffected; defensive. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\nSTATUS.md:351:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-STAGED-RESTORE-TEST-001** (open): add test case for staged-but-uncommitted prior-restore evidence in 024B-extras-2 tests (guards against future narrowing of `git diff HEAD` to `git diff`). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice.\nSTATUS.md:352:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): restore verify-phase set-equality comparison (deferred from 024B-extras-1 carve per `SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md`). Closure: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` verify phase uses jq sorted-set comparison for `required_status_checks.contexts`. NOT BLOCKING 024C — extras-1's substring grep -F is sufficient for cohort onboarding under invariant 7's <30-min SLO. Owns: 024B-extras-2 slice. Does NOT gate 024C.\nSTATUS.md:353:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-FILE-TOCTOU-001** (open): `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` reads RESTORE_PRE_STATE file three separate times (cat to RESTORE_TARGET_JSON, validate_restore_source_json, inline Python signatures extract). Mitigation: read once into a variable and pipe content to validate + signature-extract via stdin. Defensive hardening; current posture-degradation flag gates bound the blast radius. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\nSTATUS.md:354:- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-WORKFLOW-PIN-BASE-BRANCH-001** (open): `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` invokes `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` from the PR's checked-out code (PR HEAD), not the base branch. For future multi-operator adoption, pin enforcement to `git show origin/main:scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh | bash -s -- ...` or use a reusable workflow from base. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice (depth-defense); does NOT gate 024C.\ndocs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md:1280:Reference: D-047 (core restore contract), D-048 (automated Gate 3 + permanence), WP-SCP-024 invariant 7, D-035, D-030, and the break-glass guidance in `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md`.\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:207:        024A|024B-core|024B-extras|024B-extras-2|024G)\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:1708:  run_case \"$repo_dir\" 2 '' 'ERROR: --allow-not-applicable requires --tooling-slice-id <id> where <id> ∈ {024A, 024B-core, 024B-extras, 024B-extras-2, 024G}' \"\" --allow-not-applicable\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:1737:  run_case \"$repo_dir\" 2 '' 'ERROR: --allow-not-applicable requires --tooling-slice-id <id> where <id> ∈ {024A, 024B-core, 024B-extras, 024B-extras-2, 024G}' \"\" --allow-not-applicable --tooling-slice-id 024C\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:2413:  run_restore_case \"$repo_dir\" \"$fake_gh_dir\" 2 '' 'resolves outside repo root' \"$repo_dir/pre-state-link.json\"\ntests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh:3828:  run_enable_case \"$repo_dir\" \"$fake_gh_dir\" 0 'verified: adopter wrapper pins to 1111111111111111111111111111111111111111' 'WARNING: --i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible passed but wrapper is readable' --expected-wrapper-sha 1111111111111111111111111111111111111111 --i-understand-wrapper