{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_79","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,40p' STATUS.md && printf '\\\\n=====\\\\n' && sed -n '340,356p' STATUS.md && printf '\\\\n=====\\\\n' && sed -n '1260,1285p' docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md && printf '\\\\n=====\\\\n' && sed -n '118,136p' docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras-2/DISPATCH-NOTE.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Standards Control Plane — STATUS\n\n**Last updated:** 2026-05-13 (WP-SCP-024 024B-extras-2 depth-defense surface; D-048 filed)\n\n## At-a-glance\n\n| Programme | State | Track |\n|---|---|---|\n| WP-SCP-019 (Service Auth Contract) | ✅ closed 2026-04-20 | — |\n| WP-SCP-020 (Policy Federation Primitive) | ✅ **closed 2026-04-30** at v1.0.0 (Threshold A) | Track 1 |\n| WP-SCP-021 (MCP Server) | ✅ landed 2026-04-29 (USER-GATE-C signed) | Track 2 |\n| WP-SCP-022 (Implementation Programme) | ✅ **closed 2026-04-30** (USER-GATE-A signed) | Meta |\n\n## Threshold A — REACHED 2026-04-30\n\n> **Threshold A definition:** SCP gates itself on its own `main` via the federation primitive's reusable workflow with a required-status-check, all three v1.0.0 Rego rules enforcing, conflict-gate green on every PR, and a v1.0.0 release tag cut.\n\n```\n020A    plan + D-022 + D-023                                     ✅ landed\n020B    reusable workflow                                        ✅ landed (PR #36)\n020B.1  workflow-selftest harness                                ✅ landed (PR #38)\n020B.2  scripts/scp-policy-check local repro                     ✅ landed (PR #41)\n020C    starter Rego rule library (3 rules)                      ✅ landed (PR #49, 2026-04-28)\n020C.1  waiver-aware Rego + conflict-gate + read-back            ✅ landed (PR #52, 2026-04-29)\n020J    tag-protection v* + required-signed-commits              ✅ landed (PR #53, 2026-04-30) + applied\n020K    CODEOWNERS wiring (personal-account / single-operator)   ✅ landed (PR #56, 2026-04-30)\n020D1   self-dogfood wrapper merged (advisory mode)              ✅ landed (PR #57, 2026-04-30)\n020H part 1  v1.0.0-rc.1 release notes + tag cut                 ✅ landed (PR #58, 2026-04-30)\n020E.a  pre-protection canary                                    ✅ landed (PR #60, 2026-04-30)\n🛑 USER-GATE-A0  human signoff before promoting to required       ✅ signed (PR #61, 2026-04-30)\n020H part 2  promote v1.0.0-rc.1 → v1.0.0                        ✅ landed (PR #62, 2026-04-30) + tag cut\n020D2   flip gate to required (enforce_admins=true)              ✅ landed (PR #63, 2026-04-30) + applied\n020D2.1 reconciliation (D-033)                                   ✅ landed (this PR, 2026-04-30)\n🛑 USER-GATE-A  Threshold A signoff (FINISH LINE)                 ✅ **signed** (PR #64, 2026-04-30)\n```\n\n## Live operational state\n\n- `enforce_admins: true` on `main` — admin override OFF.\n- `required_status_checks: [\"policy-check / scp/policy-check\"]` (strict).\n\n=====\n## Tracked-forward items from WP-SCP-024 024B-core / 024B-extras\n\n- **FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001** (open): per-repo dispatcher install pattern resolved in ACC. install_acc_hook.sh currently hardcodes ROOT_DIR via BASH_SOURCE so each adopter repo would need its own install ceremony. 024C MUST NOT open until closed. ACC-side work item; SCP-side awaits closure. Owner: @jrnb2024.\n- **FUP-024B-CORE-NOT-APPLICABLE-WORKFLOW-001** (closed in fix-round-4; this commit): 024B-extras workflow wiring now skips script invocation entirely for tooling slices, so the residual operator-supplied `not applicable` bypass surface is gone without passing `--allow-not-applicable` or `--tooling-slice-id` into the script. Cohort cascade slices still invoke the script with full enforcement; defense-in-depth now comes from the workflow short-circuit plus the script's default refusal of `--allow-not-applicable`.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-POLICY-CHECK-TARGET-FILTER-TESTS-001** (open): add per-test coverage for `lib/policy_check_invocation.sh` target-selection loop in 024B-extras-2 (or a future slice). The loop now has 2 path-based excludes (`tests/conflict_gate/fixtures/*` + the narrowed `docs/reviews/*/r1-*.json` + siblings); no direct tests exercise these. Surfaced by R23 fix-round-23 + R24 review of fix-round-24. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-PUT-BODY-SHAPE-ASSERTIONS-001** (open): extend PUT-body shape assertions (`jq -e 'has($field) and .[$field] | type == \"boolean\"'` pattern) across ALL existing restore test cases in `tests/check_invocation_log/test_check_invocation_log_entry.sh`. Fix-round-22 added shape assertions only for the new `restore-getshape-subresources` test; the older restore tests still trust the fake-gh PUT-body acceptance without strict-shape checks. Surfaced by step-7 demo + R22 + R25 against real GitHub API (the 3rd mock-masking CRIT in this slice's history). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): `validate_restore_source_json()` `transform()` uses an exclusion-list approach — unknown GitHub branch-protection fields pass through to the PUT body. R30 surfaced `lock_branch`, `required_linear_history`, `block_creations` (and any future similar) pass through with NO posture-degradation guard, allowing a malicious pre-state to enable these without operator ack. Closure: switch to inclusion-list transform (explicitly allowed fields) + posture-degradation acknowledgement flags for each guarded sub-field. Aligns with the depth-defense surface carve (SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice (D-048); does NOT gate 024C — current exclusion list is sufficient for cohort onboarding under invariant 7's <30-min SLO since cohort pre-states are operator-captured from REAL adopter GET (not attacker-crafted).\n- **TF-024B-STEP7-DEMO-001** (closed 2026-05-11): --restore real-repo round-trip evidence at `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/restore-roundtrip-evidence.md` — operator-interactive demo at dispatch-plan step 7 completed against `jrnb2024/scp-024b-extras-restore-test` throw-away repo. **Surfaced CRIT** (mock-masking: transform did not unwrap `*.enabled` sub-objects for `required_linear_history`/`allow_force_pushes`/etc → HTTP 422 on real PUT); closed in fix-round-22 with generic `{enabled: bool}` unwrap + PUT-body-shape assertion test. Round-trip succeeded post-fix; all 4 key fields matched state-A target. Throw-away repo cleanup deferred — current gh token lacks `delete_repo` scope.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-PATH-CONTAINMENT-001** (open): apply `resolve_inside_repo_root()` guard to `scripts/enable-required-check.sh --restore <path>` argument in 024B-extras-2 alongside other defensive hardening. Low blast-radius (operator-credentials-bound). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-COHORT-REGEX-MULTICHAR-001** (open): widen `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` cohort regex from `024[C-F]/` to `024[C-F][^/]*/` for future multi-char cohort slice IDs. Current 5-cohort set (024C/D/E/F) is single-char and unaffected; defensive. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-STEP7-FIXTURE-SEQ-001** (open): align DISPATCH-NOTE step-7 fixture sequence with `restore-roundtrip-evidence-PLACEHOLDER.md` (add or harmonise `Mutate branch protection` step description). Will be resolved naturally at step-7 demo execution time.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-STAGED-RESTORE-TEST-001** (open): add test case for staged-but-uncommitted prior-restore evidence in 024B-extras-2 tests (guards against future narrowing of `git diff HEAD` to `git diff`). Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-SET-EQ-001** (closed 2026-05-13: implemented in 024B-extras-2 per D-048): restore verify-phase set-equality comparison (deferred from 024B-extras-1 carve per `SCOPE-CORRECTION-2-2026-05-11.md`). Closure: `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` verify phase uses jq sorted-set comparison for `required_status_checks.contexts`. NOT BLOCKING 024C — extras-1's substring grep -F is sufficient for cohort onboarding under invariant 7's <30-min SLO. Owns: 024B-extras-2 slice. Does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-RESTORE-FILE-TOCTOU-001** (open): `scripts/enable-required-check.sh` reads RESTORE_PRE_STATE file three separate times (cat to RESTORE_TARGET_JSON, validate_restore_source_json, inline Python signatures extract). Mitigation: read once into a variable and pipe content to validate + signature-extract via stdin. Defensive hardening; current posture-degradation flag gates bound the blast radius. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice; does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-WORKFLOW-PIN-BASE-BRANCH-001** (open): `.github/workflows/check-invocation-log-entry.yml` invokes `scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh` from the PR's checked-out code (PR HEAD), not the base branch. For future multi-operator adoption, pin enforcement to `git show origin/main:scripts/check-invocation-log-entry.sh | bash -s -- ...` or use a reusable workflow from base. Owner: 024B-extras-2 slice (depth-defense); does NOT gate 024C.\n- **TF-024B-REQCHECK-ENABLE-001** (open): Before 024C dispatch opens, operator must add `check-invocation-log-entry / check-invocation-log-entry` to main branch's `required_status_checks` list via `gh api -X PATCH repos/jrnb2024/standards-control-plane/branches/main/protection` with the updated contexts list, then record the SCP-self REQCHECK enablement as a `STATUS.md` chain entry only. Do NOT modify `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-020/branch-protection-log.md`; that log is reserved for adopter-side `enable-required-check.sh` invocations per D-035 scope. Without this step CI-enforcement is advisory only (the workflow runs but doesn't block merge). Close as part of 024C kickoff ceremony.\n- **TF-024B-SCAFFOLDER-023E002-UPDATE** (open): when TF-023E-002 closes, remove the post-v1.2.0 warning block from `scripts/scaffold-downstream.sh` and delete the cutover ancestry guard that keeps the v1.0.0 fallback recommendation alive. The scaffolder should stop warning only after the separate `attest-scorecard` workflow restructuring lands. Owner: @jrnb2024.\n\n=====\n\nIf the wrapper content cannot be read from the current context, the helper requires `--i-understand-wrapper-inaccessible` before it will continue without wrapper-pin verification.\n\nIf the wrapper has had no successful runs in the past 60 days due to extended pre-Gate-2 breakage, append `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci` to bypass the cold-start safety check (the flag's name is from the cold-start case; semantically it gates the same condition).\n\n> **Post-break-glass permanence:** After any break-glass cycle, all subsequent forward-mode `enable-required-check.sh` invocations for the same adopter permanently require `--expected-wrapper-sha` (or `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` with CAUTION audit). This is intentional: once an adopter has hit a break-glass, we demand operator-explicit SHA confirmation on every re-enable for the rest of the adopter's lifetime. The restore log entry in git history is the authoritative record; force-push to main is disabled (D-030) so the entry cannot be expunged.\n\n> **WARNING.** `--i-understand-no-gate-2-verification` is an emergency-only bypass for Gate 2. It re-arms the gate against the current wrapper SHA, so if the wrapper is still pinned to a defective SCP SHA the gate will block adopters again.\n\n```bash\nscripts/enable-required-check.sh \\\n    --repo <owner/repo> \\\n    --branch <branch> \\\n    --i-understand-no-gate-2-verification\n```\n\n> **CAUTION.** When the bypass flag is used, the helper emits a caution line in the invocation log block, prints a CAUTION line to standard error, and pauses 5 seconds before any API mutation so the operator can abort with Ctrl-C if the flag was passed unintentionally. Use it only when the operator is intentionally prioritising recovery over wrapper-pin verification.\n\n> **🛑 CAUTION:** Re-enabling required-check while the adopter wrapper is pinned to a broken/unfixed SHA will block ALL future PR merges on the adopter repo until manually unpinned. There is no scriptable rollback for this misuse - the operator must run `--restore` again with the pre-Gate-1 captured pre-state JSON.\n\nReference: D-047 (core restore contract), D-048 (automated Gate 3 + permanence), WP-SCP-024 invariant 7, D-035, D-030, and the break-glass guidance in `docs/reviews/WP-SCP-024/024B-extras/DISPATCH-NOTE.md`.\n\n## 13. Recommended Adoption Phases\n\n### Phase 0 — Prep\n\n\n=====\n| TF-024B-EXTRAS-2-TRANSFORM-INCLUSION-LIST-001 | extras-1 fix-round-31 (R30 SAFE-MAJ-001) | transform inclusion-list (replaces exclusion-list); covers lock_branch / required_linear_history / block_creations posture gap |\n\n## Slice opening checklist\n\n- [x] DISPATCH-NOTE drafted (this file)\n- [x] Branch `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-2-v2` opened off main `d7b16d0`\n- [x] Codex dispatch to apply depth-defense diff (extracted from preserved branch `feature/wp-scp-024-024b-extras-2` at fd62641 OR re-implemented from this DISPATCH-NOTE)\n- [x] 3-lens R1 review on initial implementation\n- [ ] Fix-rounds to fixpoint\n- [ ] PR + self-merge per D-040\n\nThis slice does NOT gate 024C. The cohort cascade can open in parallel once FUP-ACC-INSTALL-TARGET-REPO-001 closes (ACC-side).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
